1
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:07,910


2
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,800
Let's go!

3
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,600
Woo! Oh, the audio is doubling!

4
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,400
Both are coming through at once—

5
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,400
Whoa!

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,200
It's echoing!

7
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:53,910
Yesterday with Azuki was pretty chill, but today's not gonna be like that

8
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:55,710
I'm not taking it easy today

9
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,510
We've got this, right?

10
00:00:57,510 --> 00:00:59,510
I'm not messing around this time

11
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:04,280
Really?

12
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:08,050
Forget it, forget it

13
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:12,850
It's been a while since my last stream, so let me give a quick recap

14
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:15,650
So, today we're going to hunt the tank with Luna

15
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:16,450
Yep

16
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:18,050
Yep, that's it

17
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:18,850
That's the recap?

18
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:20,650
That was everything

19
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:23,690
That's a recap?

20
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:28,290
That's the recap

21
00:01:28,290 --> 00:01:31,120
Securing missiles

22
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:34,090
Hazard Suits

23
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:37,220
It's a mess in here

24
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:41,220
I made a bunch more rocket ammo and added it here

25
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:44,220
3, 4... 12, we've got 12

26
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:47,020
Let me grab more

27
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:49,020
I missed a lot yesterday

28
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,020
Because it got bigger

29
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:53,380
Couldn't hit it at all

30
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:57,020
Couldn't hit it?

31
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,820
Couldn't hit it

32
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,820
More food too

33
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:05,870
Food's decent at least

34
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,870
The helmets are just way too—

35
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:09,870
Tank Dismantling Center

36
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:14,470
Since we dismantle tanks, it's like a tag team burger joint

37
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:20,790
It turned into such a proper little shop

38
00:02:20,790 --> 00:02:21,690
I haven't shown this yet

39
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:23,450
You really haven't

40
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:25,170
It became a whole shop

41
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:26,730
The shop that Ponpon built

42
00:02:26,730 --> 00:02:28,650
Made quite a bit of money with this

43
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:30,310
Allow me to present

44
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:32,170
Myself

45
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:34,630
We still have 5,000 scrap

46
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:37,150
Still 5,000 scrap?

47
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:40,150
Yeah, what are we even gonna do with 5,000?

48
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:43,550
Wait, didn't we use a lot yesterday?

49
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:46,030
Guess we didn't use as much as I thought

50
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:49,030
Should we do something with it in the evening session?

51
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:52,030
We'll have to burn through 5,000 in the evening

52
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:56,630
It feels wasteful to just leave it

53
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:59,430
It's actually gone up somehow

54
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:00,430
Sorry, I kind of kept earning more

55
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,430
Yeah, I did keep adding to it

56
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:05,230
We've got materials to spare

57
00:03:05,230 --> 00:03:11,030
Before I knew it, Polka turned into a total scrap hoarder

58
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:12,030
I know, right

59
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:14,030
How much are you gonna stockpile?

60
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:16,270
We should all just—

61
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:18,910
Like, practice flying the big helicopter together

62
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:21,130
Or just all ride around in the big helicopter forever

63
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:22,610
Something like that or we'll never use it all

64
00:03:22,610 --> 00:03:25,690
As for ways to spend scrap—

65
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:28,890
You can't buy a tank, can you?

66
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:30,070
Buy a tank

67
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:31,570
Can you actually buy one?

68
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:33,590
Buying a tank would be hilarious

69
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:35,410
That's...

70
00:03:35,410 --> 00:03:36,870
Quite the idea

71
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:42,500
A boat

72
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,760
Okay, boat, boat

73
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,520
A boat, like—

74
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:49,760
Should we just make one?

75
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,620
Look

76
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,780
Here comes the boat

77
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:55,100
Okay, and—

78
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:55,920
Alright

79
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,420
It turned to night

80
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:59,720
Tonight

81
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,220
Is it morning or night?

82
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:03,820
Wait, is it going to turn to night?

83
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:08,980
It's going to get dark,

84
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,600
so let's wait until it gets light again.

85
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,340
Okay.

86
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:15,140
Is the camping car okay? Has it decayed?

87
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,940
It hasn't decayed.

88
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:17,940
Nice!

89
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,940
One car should be more than enough now, right?

90
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:24,740
You think we can manage with just this one?

91
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:25,540
Yeah, yeah.

92
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:29,540
Hold on — but don't get cocky. This is Polka we're talking about.

93
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:34,340
Just because Azuki taught us a bunch of stuff yesterday doesn't mean...

94
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:35,140
That's fair, honestly.

95
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:37,140
Right, like, we're getting a little too overconfident.

96
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:41,940
A nearly gold bag is sticking out.

97
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:48,900
No matter how much we were taught—

98
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,120
It's glowing.

99
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:54,010
Gold!

100
00:04:54,010 --> 00:04:56,910
People are worried about Luna being alone and doing fine.

101
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:59,050
That makes no sense.

102
00:04:59,050 --> 00:05:01,590
Normally there'd be someone there to protect the princess.

103
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:02,690
"Luna's fine on her own"?

104
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:04,170
What does that even mean?

105
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:07,210
But yesterday we were totally fine, for real.

106
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:09,250
Polka is really trusted, huh.

107
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:11,090
Paradoxically.

108
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:14,290
Well, yesterday we got too close to the tank.

109
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:16,070
Yeah, that's true.

110
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:18,050
We were basically right on top of it.

111
00:05:18,050 --> 00:05:20,750
Yeah, apparently we didn't need to be that close.

112
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:22,250
Right, right, right.

113
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:23,590
Hmm.

114
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:24,470
Hmm.

115
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:30,660
What would count as a win today?

116
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,680
Well, destroying the tank is a win.

117
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,680
Oh, like...

118
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,280
item-wise,

119
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:42,440
apparently the rare drops are like the L-something or M-something.

120
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,660
The M-something is the one, right.

121
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:45,440
The M-something.

122
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,200
The M249 something.

123
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:51,640
It still hasn't dropped yet,

124
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,620
and I think it's Kanatan's dream item too.

125
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,380
Yeah, it really hasn't dropped.

126
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:59,540
Right, the M249.

127
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,020
Kanatan has always been saying

128
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,740
she wants it.

129
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:06,080
The LR-300 is the only one that hasn't dropped.

130
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,960
Right, the LR-300 already dropped,

131
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:10,360
so we're going for the M249.

132
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:12,740
If the M249 drops, I think we can rest in peace.

133
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:13,720
We can finally rest in peace.

134
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:16,520
Everyone can rest in peace.

135
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:20,960
That'll prove just how powerful it is.

136
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:24,720
I wonder if it'll drop...

137
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,080
I'm gonna eat this.

138
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:27,680
Tasty.

139
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,680
Mm.

140
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:32,960
Yesterday I was totally panicking, like "this is bad, this is bad,"

141
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,620
but now I feel totally relaxed.

142
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:37,470
Wait, is that a flag?

143
00:06:37,470 --> 00:06:39,300
We've got this in the bag.

144
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,590
Do it!

145
00:06:40,590 --> 00:06:42,050
We've totally got this.

146
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:44,430
Do it! Go do the Easter Egg Hunt!

147
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:46,310
Huh?

148
00:06:46,310 --> 00:06:47,950
But there's a helicopter flying around.

149
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,390
Yeah, that's scary.

150
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:52,490
Just go without a basket or anything!

151
00:06:52,490 --> 00:06:55,780
There's a helicopter out there.

152
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,300
Huh? What's going on?

153
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:02,250
I can even hear animal sounds getting closer.

154
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:06,190
Yummy! So good!

155
00:07:06,190 --> 00:07:08,190
Is anyone here?

156
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:14,700
Seems like there should be someone...

157
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:15,500
Ha!

158
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,500
Ha!

159
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:19,020
Ha!

160
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:19,980
One.

161
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,820
Got one!

162
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,820
If we go for a one-two sweep—

163
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:26,620
there's only two of us though,

164
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:28,620
we can still get three silver eggs.

165
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:32,500
Oh, we get three?

166
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,500
Yeah, if you're in first place when no one else is around,

167
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,500
you get like three silver eggs.

168
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,500
That many?

169
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,300
Yep.

170
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:44,100
First place! Can you get first with just one egg?

171
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:49,500
Oh, but Polka was a bit slower,

172
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,500
so Polka ended up in second place.

173
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,300
Based on the timing.

174
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:55,300
So first place isn't guaranteed, huh.

175
00:07:55,300 --> 00:08:00,310


176
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:02,310
Still a little before noon.

177
00:08:02,310 --> 00:08:04,390
Okay, it's noon.

178
00:08:04,390 --> 00:08:07,390
So apparently, when the cannon fires, you crab walk.

179
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:10,380
Wait, tell me more about that!

180
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:12,410
Crab walk?

181
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:13,210
Yeah.

182
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:15,210
When the cannon fires—

183
00:08:15,210 --> 00:08:17,510
it just blasts away at you, right?

184
00:08:17,510 --> 00:08:19,570
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

185
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:27,010
When the shells come, you strafe in one direction — tap tap tap tap — and you can dodge them.

186
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:30,870
That's what both of them said yesterday too, so it really is about strafing sideways.

187
00:08:30,870 --> 00:08:33,170
Yeah, yeah, they were doing the same thing.

188
00:08:33,170 --> 00:08:35,790
Wow, pro advice!

189
00:08:35,790 --> 00:08:37,130
Step on it.

190
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:38,510
Sideways, yeah, sideways.

191
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:47,010
Sideways — don't move in both directions, just strafe one way, tap tap tap tap.

192
00:08:47,010 --> 00:08:47,840


193
00:08:57,650 --> 00:08:59,610
That's pretty cool, right?

194
00:08:59,610 --> 00:09:01,370
Wait, is the bed still there?

195
00:09:01,370 --> 00:09:01,910
Is it still over there?

196
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:10,655
We're taking the camper, let's go! I know exactly where Polka died yesterday!

197
00:09:10,655 --> 00:09:15,760
Let's go! Let's go! Yeah, let's head out! We're going!

198
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:18,610
Let's gooo! I'm getting pumped! Here we go!

199
00:09:18,610 --> 00:09:22,210
Okay — oh, are you coming out? Okay.

200
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:25,010
Oh wait! Should we take two cars?

201
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:27,610
Hm? Two cars?

202
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:29,610
Let's take two just in case.

203
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:32,410
We're feeling pretty confident though — one car should be fine at this point.

204
00:09:32,410 --> 00:09:37,210
Ah, fair enough. One car it is then. I'll leave it to you.

205
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:40,810
Alright.

206
00:09:40,810 --> 00:09:42,740
We're way too confident.

207
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:44,610
Yeah, we're way too relaxed about this.

208
00:09:44,610 --> 00:09:47,410
It'll probably be fine though.

209
00:09:47,410 --> 00:09:49,210
After yesterday's session too—

210
00:09:49,210 --> 00:09:51,210
Oh, just the one.

211
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:56,010
She probably knocked out like five or six tanks off-stream yesterday. We'll be fine.

212
00:09:56,010 --> 00:09:57,010
Eggs!

213
00:09:57,010 --> 00:09:58,810
Eggs are here? Hold on—

214
00:09:58,810 --> 00:10:00,810
Wait, hold on, Polka's gonna drop hers off too then.

215
00:10:00,810 --> 00:10:02,610
Why are you copying me?

216
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:04,610
I got three!

217
00:10:04,610 --> 00:10:05,610
Copycat!

218
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:07,410
Okay, these—

219
00:10:07,410 --> 00:10:08,210
Yep.

220
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:10,010
Stored them!

221
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:12,010
How do you get out of this thing?

222
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:14,540
You can get out with Space, right?

223
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:17,540
Yeah, Space should work. Normally.

224
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:21,180
It's not like Space ever stops working.

225
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:24,910
Why can't you get out?

226
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:29,770
Did Space suddenly break?

227
00:10:29,770 --> 00:10:39,770
Maybe if you move the car a little, the passenger seat will be accessible?

228
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:46,540
Wait, can you even get stuck in the passenger seat?

229
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:48,340
Hold on.

230
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:51,640
I can't get in.

231
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:53,190
What?

232
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:56,190
The prompt to get in isn't showing up. What's going on?

233
00:10:56,190 --> 00:10:57,990
Push push push!

234
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:02,380
Push!

235
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:04,990
Huh?

236
00:11:04,990 --> 00:11:05,790
Push!

237
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,790
Got in!

238
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,590
Looks like the position was off.

239
00:11:09,590 --> 00:11:11,590
Bad timing — that's all it was.

240
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,560
That was close!

241
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:19,460
Polka broke out in a cold sweat right then!

242
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:23,260
You were panicking too since you couldn't get in!

243
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:26,260
Alright.

244
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:31,060
The helicopter's kind of flying around nearby.

245
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:33,060
I mean...

246
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:35,860
It's kind of heading this way, but...

247
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:36,660
Yeah.

248
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:39,660
It's right on the road we need to take.

249
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,660
And we're the only ones around, so...

250
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:45,860
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8...

251
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:48,660
They're clearly targeting us!

252
00:11:48,660 --> 00:11:50,320
Obviously.

253
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,060
6, 7, 8...

254
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:54,860
I'm feeling like I could take down the helicopter right now!

255
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:56,660
We're definitely going to get shot.

256
00:11:56,660 --> 00:11:58,460
Oh, it passed us by!

257
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:00,670
It passed us by!

258
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:02,880
Are we okay?

259
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,940
We're fine.

260
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:06,820
6, 7, 8...

261
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:08,620
Nice!

262
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:11,570
Oh, a supply drop is coming down right above us.

263
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:14,220
Is it close?

264
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:17,220
We don't need supplies anymore!

265
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:24,150
Indiscriminate fire incoming!

266
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:29,890
I'm a law-abiding citizen!

267
00:12:29,890 --> 00:12:31,890
La la la la la~

268
00:12:31,890 --> 00:12:34,280
A citizen!

269
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:37,080
Wait, is it coming back?

270
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,080
Hold on!

271
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:43,800
Are you kidding me?!

272
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:46,750
Hey! Cut it out with the real missiles!

273
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:49,440
What the hell, missiles?!

274
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:52,400
Don't you dare fly off looking all satisfied with yourself!

275
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:56,200
Hey! Starting now—!

276
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:59,000
I have to eat after this, you know!

277
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,800
Are you KIDDING me?!

278
00:13:08,770 --> 00:13:10,770
That thing looked so satisfied.

279
00:13:10,770 --> 00:13:13,950
Hey, the car is completely wrecked.

280
00:13:13,950 --> 00:13:19,650
Why?!

281
