564
00:26:44,390 --> 00:26:46,390
Not a peep!

565
00:26:46,390 --> 00:26:48,190
It's super peaceful!

566
00:26:48,190 --> 00:26:51,990
Way too peaceful. What was all that stuff that killed us yesterday?

567
00:26:51,990 --> 00:26:53,990
Maybe there was never a tank here to begin with.

568
00:26:53,990 --> 00:26:55,790
Was it a hallucination?

569
00:26:55,790 --> 00:26:57,790
A hallucination~

570
00:26:57,790 --> 00:26:59,590
It was~

571
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:01,590
No way! When does it even spawn? The tank...

572
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:03,390
Spawn now! Come on, spawn already!

573
00:27:03,390 --> 00:27:05,190
Seriously though~

574
00:27:05,190 --> 00:27:06,990
For real~

575
00:27:06,990 --> 00:27:09,990
Let's at least check the rooftop.

576
00:27:09,990 --> 00:27:14,990
Let's do a quick scout.

577
00:27:14,990 --> 00:27:19,390
Anyone here?

578
00:27:19,390 --> 00:27:25,590
Has anyone beaten the tank recently?

579
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:27,590
That sounds kinda passive-aggressive.

580
00:27:27,590 --> 00:27:31,390
That came out a bit rude, didn't it.

581
00:27:31,390 --> 00:27:32,390
The spacing is like...

582
00:27:32,390 --> 00:27:34,390
easier to read, I thought.

583
00:27:36,190 --> 00:27:46,190
Someone was just here recently. Ugh. We really should've made a reservation.

584
00:27:49,810 --> 00:27:59,810
I mean, who could've seen this coming? Polka totally called it — everyone rushing the tank on the last day. Stop doing last-minute tank runs! I knew the tank was gonna be the hottest attraction today.

585
00:28:02,230 --> 00:28:03,350
Why though?!

586
00:28:03,350 --> 00:28:06,930
We should've written down time slots for the tank lol

587
00:28:06,930 --> 00:28:07,970
Reservations!

588
00:28:07,970 --> 00:28:11,010
We needed hourly reservations for this.

589
00:28:11,010 --> 00:28:13,310
Right, like, what time is your tank slot...

590
00:28:13,310 --> 00:28:16,590
Like a Pol-Luna style sign-up sheet lol

591
00:28:16,590 --> 00:28:18,810
Are you serious...

592
00:28:18,810 --> 00:28:19,430
It's over.

593
00:28:19,430 --> 00:28:20,650
Huh?!

594
00:28:20,650 --> 00:28:21,930
No way!

595
00:28:21,930 --> 00:28:23,350
It's over, Luna-san.

596
00:28:23,350 --> 00:28:23,830
The tank...

597
00:28:23,830 --> 00:28:24,510
is gone!

598
00:28:24,510 --> 00:28:26,310
Tank extermination!

599
00:28:26,310 --> 00:28:29,630
The tank lmao

600
00:28:29,630 --> 00:28:32,630
Seriously?! It's not here~

601
00:28:32,630 --> 00:28:40,530
Should've made a reservation...

602
00:28:40,530 --> 00:28:43,530
I wonder if it'll respawn if we just wait here.

603
00:28:43,530 --> 00:28:49,130
The explosion marker wasn't on the map, so it was defeated before we even logged in.

604
00:28:49,130 --> 00:28:51,930
It probably despawned after someone took it out.

605
00:28:51,930 --> 00:28:57,230
Even if it despawned after being destroyed, the question is how long ago that was.

606
00:28:57,530 --> 00:28:59,530
Yeah, how long has it been?

607
00:28:59,530 --> 00:29:02,330
That's why I asked — I want to know the timing.

608
00:29:02,330 --> 00:29:05,330
Maybe it's already gone? Nobody in this...

609
00:29:05,330 --> 00:29:09,300
One per hour? If it's one per hour, then...

610
00:29:09,300 --> 00:29:13,300
If we hope it was an hour ago, will it spawn?

611
00:29:13,300 --> 00:29:16,900
Will it spawn? Will it?

612
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:18,900
If it was an hour ago, then yeah.

613
00:29:27,370 --> 00:29:30,310
How long has it been, I wonder?

614
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:34,410
Because ever since I logged in,

615
00:29:34,410 --> 00:29:38,010
there was no explosion marker on the map.

616
00:29:38,010 --> 00:29:41,010
Oh really? I wasn't checking the map.

617
00:29:41,010 --> 00:29:47,410
4...

618
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:52,810
I see, 4 o'clock?

619
00:29:52,810 --> 00:29:55,410
Yeah, around 4:30?

620
00:29:55,410 --> 00:29:58,410
When I checked, it was already clear.

621
00:29:59,410 --> 00:30:08,460
So it was gone before that,

622
00:30:08,460 --> 00:30:13,240
but still...

623
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:18,770
Should we wait?

624
00:30:18,770 --> 00:30:20,550
I guess we'll wait.

625
00:30:20,550 --> 00:30:24,030
Will it even spawn if we wait here?

626
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:25,930
Who knows.

627
00:30:25,930 --> 00:30:27,150
Let's queue up.

628
00:30:27,150 --> 00:30:31,950
Excuse me, tank? We're next in line.

629
00:30:31,950 --> 00:30:33,550
Excuse us.

630
00:30:33,550 --> 00:30:40,290
Next, next, next — we're next for the tank.

631
00:30:40,290 --> 00:30:42,430
We're going.

632
00:30:42,430 --> 00:30:43,670
Reservation.

633
00:30:43,670 --> 00:30:46,810
Waiting in the reservation queue.

634
00:30:46,810 --> 00:30:48,890
Reserving our spot for the next tank.

635
00:30:48,890 --> 00:30:49,850
Make a reservation!

636
00:30:49,850 --> 00:30:51,690
Reserve it—

637
00:30:51,690 --> 00:30:54,130
Let's make a reservation.

638
00:30:54,130 --> 00:30:57,050
When it's a once-an-hour attraction,

639
00:30:57,050 --> 00:30:58,250
people are gonna

640
00:30:58,250 --> 00:31:01,570
flock to it.

641
00:31:01,570 --> 00:31:02,790
Looks like it.

642
00:31:02,790 --> 00:31:03,950
No way.

643
00:31:03,950 --> 00:31:05,510
Seriously, no way.

644
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:08,370
I didn't think anyone would be here at this hour.

645
00:31:08,370 --> 00:31:09,550
This is bad.

646
00:31:09,550 --> 00:31:12,070
We didn't make a reservation for the tank.

647
00:31:12,070 --> 00:31:15,030
Looks like tank reservation day has

648
00:31:15,030 --> 00:31:16,290
arrived.

649
00:31:16,290 --> 00:31:18,670
People are probably waking up in the morning like "time to do the tank!"

650
00:31:18,670 --> 00:31:21,790
I thought we could just go right away.

651
00:31:21,790 --> 00:31:25,590
But those other players who are pros —

652
00:31:25,590 --> 00:31:29,390
do they even still feel the joy of getting the loot?

653
00:31:29,390 --> 00:31:31,140
Do they even remember it?

654
00:31:31,140 --> 00:31:33,790
I dunno.

655
00:31:33,790 --> 00:31:35,790
They can't possibly use everything they get.

656
00:31:35,790 --> 00:31:38,480
Does everyone really want to do the tank that badly?

657
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:41,190
I heard the tank gives the best loot though.

658
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:42,190
Oh really?

659
00:31:42,190 --> 00:31:44,990
How was it actually? Yesterday — good loot?

660
00:31:44,990 --> 00:31:48,990
Well... I mean... yeah, sort of.

661
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:54,390
I'm not sure since we didn't get any rares.

662
00:31:54,390 --> 00:31:56,390
Do rocket launcher ammo drops come out of it?

663
00:31:56,390 --> 00:31:59,390
Oh yeah, yeah! Ammo did drop — rocket launcher ammo.

664
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:05,190
Like, "here's more rockets, go blow up another tank" kind of thing?

665
00:32:05,190 --> 00:32:07,190
It never ends.

666
00:32:07,190 --> 00:32:10,790
That's why people can't help but keep farming it.

667
00:32:10,790 --> 00:32:15,590
I see — so I've opened up reservations, feel free to book a slot.

668
00:32:15,590 --> 00:32:16,910
We did make a reservation this time though.

669
00:32:16,910 --> 00:32:19,090
People just logging in now definitely have no idea about that.

670
00:32:19,090 --> 00:32:24,790
Like, why would you even farm this at this point?

671
00:32:24,790 --> 00:32:26,010
No no no no.

672
00:32:26,010 --> 00:32:27,810
It's because it's today, that's exactly why.

673
00:32:27,810 --> 00:32:29,390
Huh?

674
00:32:29,390 --> 00:32:32,610
People might come precisely because it's today.

675
00:32:32,610 --> 00:32:34,910
Ahh, like they keep pulling the gacha...

676
00:32:34,910 --> 00:32:39,250
Right, and today's the last day, so there are tons of people who want to experience the final tank fight.

677
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:39,850
The final...

678
00:32:39,850 --> 00:32:42,530
Today is the last day of PVE, after all.

679
00:32:42,530 --> 00:32:44,430
One last time.

680
00:32:44,430 --> 00:32:45,890
For the memories.

681
00:32:45,890 --> 00:32:48,010
Everyone wants to do the tank one more time.

682
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:49,310
That's true.

683
00:32:49,310 --> 00:32:50,690
A commemorative tank run.

684
00:32:50,690 --> 00:32:53,830
They want to do a commemorative tank farm.

685
00:32:53,830 --> 00:32:54,710
Exactly.

686
00:32:54,710 --> 00:32:58,790
For anyone just joining — to explain:

687
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,770
we went to go defeat the tank,

688
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:01,290
and the tank

689
00:33:01,290 --> 00:33:03,290
wasn't there.

690
00:33:03,290 --> 00:33:06,580
So for now,

691
00:33:06,580 --> 00:33:08,760
we can at least look around.

692
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:12,360
I'm not even sure where it wanders.

693
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:13,660
We didn't go inside at all.

694
00:33:13,660 --> 00:33:16,160
We were shooting from way outside earlier.

695
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:17,760
Yeah, like...

696
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:18,960
Azukichi probably

697
00:33:18,960 --> 00:33:23,160
told us to fight it from a distance.

698
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:26,370
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

699
00:33:26,370 --> 00:33:27,770
So if the tank spawns roughly every hour,

700
00:33:27,770 --> 00:33:30,070
thinking about it as one hour intervals...

701
00:33:30,070 --> 00:33:31,070
there are about 8 more chances.

702
00:33:31,070 --> 00:33:33,170
"About 8 more" — that's kind of funny.

703
00:33:33,170 --> 00:33:35,570
Every single tank slot might already be taken.

704
00:33:35,570 --> 00:33:38,230
True — first come, first served.

705
00:33:38,230 --> 00:33:39,210
Ha!

706
00:33:39,210 --> 00:33:42,190
There might be someone out there who's dead set on

707
00:33:42,190 --> 00:33:44,850
doing every single tank spawn.

708
00:33:44,850 --> 00:33:46,130
You think?

709
00:33:46,130 --> 00:33:47,090
First come, first served.

710
00:33:47,090 --> 00:33:48,450
Maybe 4 o'clock? What do you think?

711
00:33:48,450 --> 00:33:50,150
Do you think it'll spawn at 4?

712
00:33:50,150 --> 00:33:51,470
Huh, why?

713
00:33:51,470 --> 00:33:55,070
I wonder who took it down and when.

714
00:33:55,070 --> 00:33:57,150
When we logged in...

715
00:33:57,150 --> 00:33:58,410
Hmm, hmm...

716
00:33:58,410 --> 00:34:00,250
Was it after they finished?

717
00:34:00,250 --> 00:34:02,570
But if it was after they finished,

718
00:34:02,570 --> 00:34:06,150
when Polka checked the map,

719
00:34:06,150 --> 00:34:07,670
it was already...

720
00:34:07,670 --> 00:34:11,250
it might spawn again pretty soon?

721
00:34:11,250 --> 00:34:12,410
Hmm...

722
00:34:12,410 --> 00:34:17,010
I'm hoping it will.

723
00:34:17,010 --> 00:34:20,390
We were shooting from around here yesterday too.

724
00:34:20,390 --> 00:34:22,690
I see.

725
00:34:22,690 --> 00:34:24,150
So this spot works fine.

726
00:34:24,150 --> 00:34:25,790
The shells were flying right past us.

727
00:34:25,790 --> 00:34:27,890
It got stuck over there, right?

728
00:34:27,890 --> 00:34:30,790
Around NE50.

729
00:34:30,790 --> 00:34:32,330
So they can get stuck too, huh.

730
00:34:32,330 --> 00:34:35,350
It got stuck and wouldn't move at all,

731
00:34:35,350 --> 00:34:38,290
so we just kept shooting it there.

732
00:34:38,290 --> 00:34:39,830
Get stuck for us!

733
00:34:39,830 --> 00:34:42,690
Oh, does a notification pop up when it spawns?

734
00:34:42,690 --> 00:34:43,990
Ah!

735
00:34:43,990 --> 00:34:47,630
Yeah, come to think of it, a red one shows up.

736
00:34:47,630 --> 00:34:49,830
Something like "[X] has respawned."

737
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:51,150
What does the tank show up as in the notification?

738
00:34:51,150 --> 00:34:52,550
Is it like "CH" something?

739
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:54,230
It shows something like "CH whatever," right?

740
00:34:54,230 --> 00:34:56,830
I wonder what it says for the tank.

741
00:34:56,830 --> 00:34:59,720
I'm not sure.

742
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,960
The ones I always see are—

743
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,700
there's one I can never figure out.

744
00:35:03,700 --> 00:35:06,420
There's the Cargo Ship...

745
00:35:06,420 --> 00:35:11,640
Is the Cargo Ship the tank?

746
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:14,100
Hmm, I wonder.

747
00:35:14,100 --> 00:35:16,000
"Cargo" does kind of sound tank-like.

748
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,720
CH is the supply helicopter.

749
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:21,460
Oh, so the tank doesn't get an announcement?

750
00:35:21,460 --> 00:35:23,060
Cargo Ship is the boat.

751
00:35:23,060 --> 00:35:25,220
Right, "ship" would be the boat.

752
00:35:25,220 --> 00:35:27,600
Tank, please come online!

753
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:29,660
Today the tank has also come online!

754
00:35:29,660 --> 00:35:30,380
Make an announcement!

755
00:35:30,380 --> 00:35:33,180
Tank, please go online!

756
00:35:33,180 --> 00:35:34,800
Ma'am, please spawn the tank!

757
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:37,260
That's asking a lot.

758
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:40,720
I need the tank right now!

759
00:35:40,720 --> 00:35:41,800
Please give us a tank!

760
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:42,520
Sure, why not.

761
00:35:42,520 --> 00:35:44,320
Spawn like two of them, please.

762
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,120
Sure thing.

763
00:35:46,120 --> 00:35:48,120
Bold request.

764
00:35:48,120 --> 00:35:54,900
When the tank logs in, make a proper announcement that it's online.

765
00:35:54,900 --> 00:35:56,900
I hope it shows up...

766
00:35:56,900 --> 00:36:00,500
Should we wait until 4 o'clock?

767
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:02,300
I guess that's all we can do.

768
00:36:02,300 --> 00:36:04,300
Let's make some fun conversation in the meantime.

769
00:36:04,300 --> 00:36:08,100
So, looking back on this final stretch — how was it?

770
00:36:08,100 --> 00:36:10,900
It went by so fast!

771
00:36:10,900 --> 00:36:18,340
Luna even rearranged her work schedule to play during this period.

772
00:36:18,340 --> 00:36:27,240
Well, at first I was worried whether I could set up the whole farming system in just one week,

773
00:36:27,240 --> 00:36:31,560
but it went pretty smoothly overall.

774
00:36:32,760 --> 00:36:39,760
In the second half, Polka helped out and we got a huge haul of pumpkins.

775
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:46,560
I honestly never expected to be taking care of pumpkins myself. Even I'm surprised.

776
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:52,160
Truly. We worked on it together.

777
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:55,760
She's already doing the closing speech.

778
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:59,760
Pre-booking the closing — reserving the sign-off in advance.

779
00:36:59,760 --> 00:37:02,760
I figured I'd get the closing out of the way early.

780
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:05,560
Today's order of events is all over the place.

781
00:37:05,560 --> 00:37:08,360
Like, might as well do the sign-off now.

782
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:11,500
Starting with the farewell speech—

783
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:13,500
What kind of stream starts with the farewell speech?

784
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:18,300
Is there anything else fun to do here while we wait for the tank?

785
00:37:18,300 --> 00:37:21,100
Hmm... not really.

786
00:37:21,100 --> 00:37:27,500
I heard there's a recycler here,

787
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:30,300
but I want something actually fun to do.

788
00:37:30,300 --> 00:37:33,100
There's nothing here.

789
00:37:33,100 --> 00:37:35,900
It's going to get dark soon.

790
00:37:35,900 --> 00:37:40,700
Once it's night it'll be lonely, cold, dark — we won't know what's going on.

791
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:43,500
We'll have no choice but to retreat to the camping car.

792
00:37:43,500 --> 00:37:46,300
Then let's just camp in the camping car.

793
00:37:46,300 --> 00:37:47,780
Should we try to take down the helicopter?

794
00:37:47,780 --> 00:37:52,260
Can we even do that?

795
00:37:52,260 --> 00:37:55,160
I don't really know how to deal with the helicopter either.

796
00:37:55,160 --> 00:38:00,820
If you picked up meat, cook it in the camping car.

797
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:03,160
Oh, the meat.

798
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:05,060
But I don't have any wood.

799
00:38:05,060 --> 00:38:07,880
I brought wood.

800
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:09,460
Then cook the meat!

801
00:38:09,460 --> 00:38:12,380
Can you even cook in the camping car?

802
00:38:12,380 --> 00:38:15,180
Hard to get out of the camping car. Open up!

803
00:38:15,180 --> 00:38:16,880
Where did we park the car again?

804
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:17,780
Over there.

805
00:38:17,780 --> 00:38:19,780
Over there.

806
00:38:19,780 --> 00:38:23,080
It's the camping car! Open up!

807
00:38:23,080 --> 00:38:23,980
This one.

808
00:38:23,980 --> 00:38:26,680
Guess we're roughing it out here.

809
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:32,180
Oh, we can cook here?

810
00:38:32,180 --> 00:38:35,890
Oh wow, we can!

811
00:38:35,890 --> 00:38:39,490
Wood.

812
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:43,310
Can we cook?

813
00:38:43,310 --> 00:38:44,640
Oh, it's cooking!

814
00:38:44,640 --> 00:38:45,540
Huh?

815
00:38:45,540 --> 00:38:48,740
Isn't it dangerous to cook inside the car?

816
00:38:48,740 --> 00:38:53,370
But that's kind of the whole point of a camping car.

817
00:38:53,370 --> 00:38:55,170
What?!

818
00:38:55,170 --> 00:38:58,070
We're gonna get carbon monoxide poisoning.

819
00:38:58,070 --> 00:39:00,070
Open a window, open a window!

820
00:39:00,070 --> 00:39:01,370
We're gonna get carbon monoxide poisoning!

821
00:39:01,370 --> 00:39:03,870
I said open a window!

822
00:39:03,870 --> 00:39:08,000
All windows are sealed shut.

823
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:14,900
Right? Scary. And the meat is raw — we haven't picked any up, have we?

824
00:39:14,900 --> 00:39:21,280
I didn't bring any meat. I'm just burning stuff for no reason.

825
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:25,000
Oh, you're grabbing ammo. Getting ammo right now.

826
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:30,520
Oh, I accidentally threw a grenade. Why did I throw a grenade?!

827
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:35,220
Stop that! Please don't throw grenades inside the car!

828
00:39:35,220 --> 00:39:38,600
I thought we were about to explode.

829
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:45,040
Please stop. But it's way too peaceful — will the tank actually spawn?

830
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:50,460
Does it even sync up with real-world time?

831
00:39:50,460 --> 00:39:54,140
No idea. Who knows. Oh—

832
00:39:54,140 --> 00:39:56,760
Oh, you scared me! What was that?

833
00:39:56,760 --> 00:40:00,660
That was just a car sound from outside.

834
00:40:00,660 --> 00:40:03,420
Did it spawn?

835
00:40:03,420 --> 00:40:05,980
That was a car near Polka in real life.

836
00:40:05,980 --> 00:40:09,240
There's one spawning near Polka too!

837
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:12,850
The tank!

838
00:40:12,850 --> 00:40:15,230
It's getting dark out...

839
00:40:15,230 --> 00:40:19,030
No no no, not nighttime, please!

840
00:40:19,030 --> 00:40:23,910
Night is a bit dangerous, so let's wait until daytime.

841
00:40:23,990 --> 00:40:31,130
You can see the fire from outside too.

842
00:40:31,130 --> 00:40:35,050
The detail in this game is incredible.

843
00:40:35,050 --> 00:40:40,750
Popo is burning charcoal indoors.

844
00:40:40,750 --> 00:40:46,770
Making charcoal right now. How's it going? Hear anything yet?

845
00:40:46,770 --> 00:40:51,570
I mean, we're literally inside enemy territory right now,

846
00:40:51,570 --> 00:40:55,910
so it could spawn any time.

847
00:40:55,910 --> 00:41:01,720
This car could get blown up too.

848
00:41:01,720 --> 00:41:09,480
I don't hear anything at all.

849
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:17,740
Maybe it hasn't respawned yet. Still about 5 more minutes — the tank's probably being built right now.

850
00:41:17,740 --> 00:41:22,980
Hopefully it's being built as we speak.

851
00:41:24,420 --> 00:41:28,920
We just can't seem to get a good fight with the tank, can we?

852
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:31,420
Since yesterday...

853
00:41:31,420 --> 00:41:33,120
Yeah, seriously.

854
00:41:33,120 --> 00:41:38,020
Polka's been looking forward to it since Luna said she learned the tricks.

855
00:41:38,020 --> 00:41:39,220
Right, for real.

856
00:41:39,220 --> 00:41:44,920
I was hoping we'd get to see some heroics today, but the timing just isn't working out.

857
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:47,720
Yeah, the timing just isn't lining up.

858
00:41:47,720 --> 00:41:50,320
Is it because we lit the fire? Our comfort level went up.

859
00:41:50,320 --> 00:41:51,720
It was at 50% yesterday.

860
00:41:51,720 --> 00:41:52,620
Oh, you're right!

861
00:41:53,020 --> 00:41:55,390
It's actually comfortable in here.

862
00:41:55,390 --> 00:41:56,880
Right?

863
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,860
This is comfortable?

864
00:41:58,860 --> 00:42:03,100
An airdrop came down, but...

865
00:42:03,100 --> 00:42:06,560
What about our...

866
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:09,400
What about our tank?

867
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:11,200
The tank should drop down too—

868
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:13,600
Still being manufactured.

869
00:42:13,600 --> 00:42:17,360
Does it spawn by dropping from the sky like an ARK dinosaur?

870
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:18,820
Who knows.

871
00:42:18,820 --> 00:42:20,920
With the tank, I mean.

872
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:24,560
We did start with a crash landing yesterday.

873
00:42:24,560 --> 00:42:28,040
Yesterday was rough.

874
00:42:28,040 --> 00:42:30,000
It was basically a zombie attack.

875
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:32,640
That was totally unnecessary.

876
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:38,090
It's night.

877
00:42:38,090 --> 00:42:39,750
It's nighttime.

878
00:42:39,750 --> 00:42:43,070
Come on, spawn already!

879
00:42:43,070 --> 00:42:50,920
I got an Instagram notification.

880
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:54,960
No matter when or where, Instagram must be checked.

881
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:55,960
Oh, morning—

882
00:42:56,020 --> 00:42:57,820
Is something going to spawn?

883
00:42:57,820 --> 00:43:01,010
Something's spawning.

884
00:43:01,010 --> 00:43:03,010
Come on, tank, spawn already!

885
00:43:03,010 --> 00:43:04,780
Seriously.

886
00:43:04,780 --> 00:43:06,610
Eggs spawned.

887
00:43:06,610 --> 00:43:08,610
Isn't the Easter event every hour?

888
00:43:08,610 --> 00:43:10,410
If so, it's already been an hour.

889
00:43:10,410 --> 00:43:12,410
Wait, but—

890
00:43:12,410 --> 00:43:14,210
Does it reset from when you defeat the tank,

891
00:43:14,210 --> 00:43:16,210
or from when it spawns?

892
00:43:16,210 --> 00:43:18,010
Oh, the Easter event?

893
00:43:18,010 --> 00:43:20,010
Is Easter every hour?

894
00:43:20,010 --> 00:43:21,810
I'm not sure how Easter works.

895
00:43:21,810 --> 00:43:23,610
If it is, then yeah, an hour's passed.

896
00:43:23,610 --> 00:43:25,610
Timing-wise, it's been about an hour.

897
00:43:25,610 --> 00:43:26,610
Right.

898
00:43:26,610 --> 00:43:35,960
The worst would be if we're collecting eggs right where the tank is, and it suddenly shows up and just unloads on us.

899
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:37,160
True.

900
00:43:37,160 --> 00:43:39,160
Which one is whose?

901
00:43:39,160 --> 00:43:43,290
Is it not here?

902
00:43:43,290 --> 00:43:47,600
No tank?

903
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:50,840
Is that a helicopter?

904
00:43:50,840 --> 00:43:53,640
That's not the tank's sound.

905
00:43:56,240 --> 00:43:58,060
Why isn't it here?

906
00:43:58,060 --> 00:44:02,040
The tank sounds way more aggressive than that.

907
00:44:02,040 --> 00:44:04,640
What is that sound?

908
00:44:04,640 --> 00:44:06,640
That's probably just something flying overhead.

909
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:08,640
Something flying overhead, huh.

910
00:44:08,640 --> 00:44:17,820
The tank has this sound that screams "I'm coming for you" — you can feel the hostility even the first time you hear it.

911
00:44:17,820 --> 00:44:18,620
Yeah.

912
00:44:18,620 --> 00:44:22,220
Even hearing it for the first time, you could tell it meant business.

913
00:44:22,220 --> 00:44:25,020
Should we go look for it again?

914
00:44:25,020 --> 00:44:28,860
But the tank was already here when we arrived last time.

915
00:44:28,860 --> 00:44:29,780
It was here yesterday.

916
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:30,240
It was.

917
00:44:30,240 --> 00:44:31,300
We took it down.

918
00:44:31,300 --> 00:44:33,020
How did the practice run go yesterday?

919
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:35,740
We took it down during practice too.

920
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:41,720
This is literally the tank's patrol route,

921
00:44:41,720 --> 00:44:46,600
so it's weird that it's not here.

922
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,820
Exactly.

923
00:44:48,820 --> 00:44:55,920
Could it be that we can't tell unless we move away?

924
00:45:00,290 --> 00:45:03,550
Maybe we can't tell if we stay in one spot.

925
00:45:03,550 --> 00:45:05,770
Like, there'd be a notification saying it spawned,

926
00:45:05,770 --> 00:45:07,270
since we've been getting all kinds of notifications.

927
00:45:07,270 --> 00:45:10,610
I don't think that's how it works though.

928
00:45:10,610 --> 00:45:11,690
Hmm.

929
00:45:11,690 --> 00:45:12,890
Ponpon, Unataan—

930
00:45:12,890 --> 00:45:13,770
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

931
00:45:13,770 --> 00:45:17,100
Got it.

932
00:45:17,100 --> 00:45:22,590
So, Polka has to step away for a bit tonight,

933
00:45:22,590 --> 00:45:26,390
I have to log off for a while in the evening,

934
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:29,330
right during prime time—

935
00:45:29,330 --> 00:45:31,410
I can't be here for prime time,

936
00:45:31,410 --> 00:45:32,790
which is why it ended up being this time slot.

937
00:45:32,790 --> 00:45:35,250
But when I come back,

938
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:37,610
today as well—

939
00:45:37,610 --> 00:45:40,670
the PVE period runs

940
00:45:40,670 --> 00:45:41,910
until midnight,

941
00:45:41,910 --> 00:45:42,750
so the server should be open,

942
00:45:42,750 --> 00:45:44,750
and I'd love to stream again if I can.

943
00:45:44,750 --> 00:45:47,390


944
00:45:47,390 --> 00:45:50,170
I'm hoping to stream again if possible.

945
00:45:50,170 --> 00:45:50,790
Polkan—

946
00:45:50,790 --> 00:45:52,810
I think Kanatan feels the same way.

947
00:45:52,810 --> 00:45:54,860
Why?

948
00:45:54,860 --> 00:45:56,860
Let's enjoy it

949
00:45:56,860 --> 00:45:58,980
right to the very end.

950
00:45:58,980 --> 00:46:03,610
But yeah,

951
00:46:03,610 --> 00:46:05,730
the tank still hasn't respawned.

952
00:46:05,730 --> 00:46:07,590
Yep.

953
00:46:07,590 --> 00:46:10,030
Polka has really been in Luna's care a lot this time around,

954
00:46:10,030 --> 00:46:12,390
and the Troupe members too —

955
00:46:12,390 --> 00:46:14,970
probably more than I even realize.

956
00:46:14,970 --> 00:46:17,490


957
00:46:17,490 --> 00:46:19,070
But in return,

958
00:46:19,070 --> 00:46:20,530
it's been so much fun.

959
00:46:20,530 --> 00:46:22,530
It really has.

960
00:46:22,530 --> 00:46:24,790
Thank you so much for having us.

961
00:46:24,790 --> 00:46:30,770
I'm not sure what'll happen during PVP, but...

962
00:46:30,770 --> 00:46:40,770
Polka really had a great time staying with Luna.

963
00:46:42,890 --> 00:46:52,890
When I was lost and overwhelmed on my own, Luna invited me to live with her, and I was so grateful.

964
00:46:55,330 --> 00:46:58,020
I was really thankful for that—

965
00:46:58,020 --> 00:46:59,810
They're here!

966
00:46:59,810 --> 00:47:01,810
Luna's here!

967
00:47:01,810 --> 00:47:06,220
Luna, where are you?

968
00:47:06,220 --> 00:47:09,220
She's here!

969
00:47:09,220 --> 00:47:17,240
The tank spawned!

970
00:47:17,240 --> 00:47:23,640
Wait, what? It spawned?

971
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:30,750
It spawned!

972
00:47:30,750 --> 00:47:32,750
I'm dead though.

973
00:47:32,550 --> 00:47:35,010
Huh?! What? What? What?

974
00:47:35,010 --> 00:47:39,950
Hey! I was in the bathroom — can you NOT do this right now?!

975
00:47:39,950 --> 00:47:42,090
Oh no, Luna's in the red! What?!

976
00:47:42,090 --> 00:47:46,990
Are you kidding me?!

977
00:47:46,990 --> 00:47:52,910
Luna! Luna?! Luna, did you not set a bed here?

978
00:47:52,910 --> 00:47:56,690
Ugh! Wait, the bathroom— ugh!

979
00:47:56,690 --> 00:47:58,690
What do I do?

980
00:47:58,690 --> 00:48:00,690
Oh no— Luna!

981
00:48:00,690 --> 00:48:04,690
What do I do?!

982
00:48:04,690 --> 00:48:06,690
Why?!

983
00:48:06,690 --> 00:48:10,690
Huh?!

984
00:48:10,690 --> 00:48:12,690
Wait, why NOW?!

985
00:48:12,690 --> 00:48:14,690
What?!

986
00:48:14,690 --> 00:48:16,690
What?!

987
00:48:16,690 --> 00:48:20,690
I didn't even do anything!

988
00:48:20,690 --> 00:48:22,690
And on top of that, what is happening?!

989
00:48:26,430 --> 00:48:28,370
My main character got hit by a missile and died.

990
00:48:28,370 --> 00:48:30,550
The tank is doing its job, I'll give it that.

991
00:48:30,550 --> 00:48:33,390
But I didn't even hear the tank...

992
00:48:33,720 --> 00:48:35,320
Why?

993
00:48:35,320 --> 00:48:41,520
I was just talking about how great it's been staying with Luna, and then this happens.

994
00:48:41,520 --> 00:48:44,120
I didn't hear it at all!

995
00:48:44,120 --> 00:48:49,520
I come back and everyone's dead — what is going on?

996
00:48:49,520 --> 00:48:55,120
Hey tank, seriously, stop ghosting us. Were you watching the stream?

997
00:48:55,120 --> 00:48:56,620
Stop ghosting us.

998
00:48:56,620 --> 00:48:57,320
It really picked its moment.

999
00:48:57,320 --> 00:49:01,920
Hey, there's an airdrop that looks like it landed pretty close by.

1000
00:49:01,920 --> 00:49:05,660
Ugh, why are we dead?! What the heck?!

1001
00:49:05,660 --> 00:49:10,120
Can you get here? Should we split stuff from the car?

1002
00:49:10,120 --> 00:49:14,100
I'm not registered to the car so nothing shows up.

1003
00:49:14,100 --> 00:49:15,900
Uh, the sleeping bag—

1004
00:49:15,900 --> 00:49:20,740
So what should Polka bring, and where should I go?

1005
00:49:20,740 --> 00:49:24,940
I think there's a sleeping bag around J-7.

1006
00:49:24,940 --> 00:49:27,440
J-7?

1007
00:49:27,440 --> 00:49:35,980
Yeah, same area as yesterday — I think I set a bed there.

1008
00:49:35,980 --> 00:49:43,140
Hey Luna, I set a bed for you in the car — what do you think?

1009
00:49:43,140 --> 00:49:52,480
It's grayed out and I can't select it — says it's in use. I just got out of the car.

1010
00:49:52,480 --> 00:49:59,640
What about clothes? Clothes? There are some up top, put them on quick.

1011
00:49:59,640 --> 00:50:04,880
No Hazard Suit in here. Up top, the closet.

1012
00:50:04,880 --> 00:50:09,180
Where? Up, up, up — found it!

1013
00:50:09,180 --> 00:50:13,410
I thought I was gonna die. Well, I did die.

1014
00:50:13,410 --> 00:50:16,760
Hey, wait — isn't this seriously messed up?

1015
00:50:16,760 --> 00:50:19,760
Attacking someone while they're in the bathroom is the worst.

1016
00:50:19,760 --> 00:50:22,260
Did you eat? Did you eat anything?

1017
00:50:22,260 --> 00:50:24,760
I haven't eaten.

1018
00:50:24,760 --> 00:50:28,760
Please stop attacking me while I'm in the bathroom.

1019
00:50:28,760 --> 00:50:30,760
Where are you? Hold on—

1020
00:50:30,760 --> 00:50:36,560
Weren't you feeling a little safe too?

1021
00:50:36,560 --> 00:50:38,560
How did this even happen?

1022
00:50:38,560 --> 00:50:41,360
And of all times, right at the end—

1023
00:50:41,360 --> 00:50:44,360
I said I was going to the bathroom at the very end—

1024
00:50:44,360 --> 00:50:47,320
Maybe that wasn't the best time to go, huh?

1025
00:50:47,320 --> 00:50:50,580
I didn't think it would show up then!

1026
00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:53,140
That scared me!

1027
00:50:53,140 --> 00:50:56,280
I need to go recover my stuff.

1028
00:50:56,280 --> 00:50:58,260
Are you okay?

1029
00:50:58,260 --> 00:51:00,210
I'll come with you, I'll come with you.

1030
00:51:00,210 --> 00:51:02,920
I want to go get my stuff back.

1031
00:51:02,920 --> 00:51:04,520
This is the worst.

1032
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:06,200
This is kind of funny though.

1033
00:51:06,200 --> 00:51:09,620
That tank knew exactly what it was doing.

1034
00:51:09,620 --> 00:51:11,620
What is even happening?

1035
00:51:11,620 --> 00:51:13,620
Why did it spawn so suddenly?

1036
00:51:13,620 --> 00:51:15,620
It was just time for it to spawn.

1037
00:51:15,620 --> 00:51:21,040
Where's my stuff?

1038
00:51:21,040 --> 00:51:22,040
Can't heal without a rat or something.

1039
00:51:22,040 --> 00:51:23,930
Oh, I can hear it!

1040
00:51:23,930 --> 00:51:27,920
Wait, I need to eat something to recover health.

1041
00:51:27,920 --> 00:51:29,720
Okay, okay, okay!

1042
00:51:29,720 --> 00:51:32,820
Wait, the rat-something—

1043
00:51:32,820 --> 00:51:34,820
I can hear it!

1044
00:51:34,820 --> 00:51:39,200
Alright—

1045
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:41,200
Let me drink some water too.

1046
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:46,890
I had tea, so I should be fine on water.

1047
00:51:46,890 --> 00:51:52,590
Seriously though, what?! I missed the moment it got destroyed!

1048
00:51:52,590 --> 00:51:55,700
But the Lunaitos probably saw it, right?

1049
00:51:55,700 --> 00:52:02,490
Well, I had the escape menu open on my end...

1050
00:52:02,490 --> 00:52:06,690
What happened? Polka was doing the whole emotional closing bit too.

1051
00:52:06,690 --> 00:52:09,590
Apparently I only heard the sound.

1052
00:52:09,590 --> 00:52:12,770
I should've told you to get somewhere safe first.

1053
00:52:12,770 --> 00:52:18,250
I totally thought it wasn't coming yet.

1054
00:52:18,250 --> 00:52:19,550
You'd think it wasn't coming!

1055
00:52:19,550 --> 00:52:23,210
Luna's been through so much — you practiced yesterday, right?

1056
00:52:23,210 --> 00:52:25,250
I mean, the whole time—

1057
00:52:25,250 --> 00:52:27,190
You should've practiced taking bathroom breaks too!

1058
00:52:27,190 --> 00:52:29,890
You weren't even there!

1059
00:52:29,890 --> 00:52:33,050
Seriously, where did I even die?

1060
00:52:33,050 --> 00:52:36,520
Is Pen-chan here?

1061
00:52:36,520 --> 00:52:39,600
Yeah, I can hear something from the north.

1062
00:52:39,600 --> 00:52:43,220
Polka's body should be around here somewhere.

1063
00:52:43,220 --> 00:52:45,180
Found it! I died here.

1064
00:52:45,180 --> 00:52:48,300
There's the death marker.

1065
00:52:48,300 --> 00:52:52,900
Good, that spot looks safe.

1066
00:52:52,900 --> 00:52:55,860
Grab it quick!

1067
00:52:55,860 --> 00:52:58,140
I don't hear much right now.

1068
00:52:58,140 --> 00:53:00,640
It's north, but I can still hear it.

1069
00:53:00,640 --> 00:53:06,380
Okay, let's fall back and sort out our stuff.

1070
00:53:06,380 --> 00:53:07,800
It's moving away.

1071
00:53:07,800 --> 00:53:09,700
But it's definitely coming this way.

1072
00:53:09,700 --> 00:53:10,750
This is terrifying.

1073
00:53:10,750 --> 00:53:12,780
Seriously, no way...

1074
00:53:12,780 --> 00:53:18,620
Don't do anything funny!

1075
00:53:18,620 --> 00:53:21,460
Why did you open the options menu?!

1076
00:53:21,460 --> 00:53:24,680
It doesn't matter either way!

1077
00:53:24,680 --> 00:53:27,680
Let me see how you died!

1078
00:53:27,680 --> 00:53:29,660
I had it on a background screen—

1079
00:53:29,660 --> 00:53:31,800
I walked right past it with the escape menu still open.

1080
00:53:31,800 --> 00:53:33,300
Ugh!

1081
00:53:33,300 --> 00:53:36,780
It shouldn't matter which screen you're on!

1082
00:53:37,940 --> 00:53:39,940
Well, it spawned, so that's good.

1083
00:53:39,940 --> 00:53:40,940
Yeah, true.

1084
00:53:40,940 --> 00:53:46,340
Alright, we're good to go!

1085
00:53:46,340 --> 00:53:47,140
Where is it?

1086
00:53:47,140 --> 00:53:49,940
Luna, where'd you go?

1087
00:53:49,940 --> 00:53:51,940
She's already inside — wait, she went in?!

1088
00:53:51,940 --> 00:53:52,740
What?!

1089
00:53:52,740 --> 00:53:57,390
Yesterday with Azuki and the others, around this area—

1090
00:53:57,390 --> 00:53:58,390
You went that far in?

1091
00:53:58,390 --> 00:54:03,790
Around here, near the right entrance.

1092
00:54:03,790 --> 00:54:04,790
There's a good spot there.

1093
00:54:06,590 --> 00:54:07,390
Is it there?

1094
00:54:07,390 --> 00:54:11,190
Yes, yes, yes! I can hear it clearly!

1095
00:54:11,190 --> 00:54:13,990
Wait, is Polka closer? NW—

1096
00:54:13,990 --> 00:54:15,790
NNW.

1097
00:54:15,790 --> 00:54:19,590
Oh, I see it! Visual, visual, visual!

1098
00:54:19,590 --> 00:54:25,190
Visual, NWN, 340.

1099
00:54:25,190 --> 00:54:29,100
NW, this way?

1100
00:54:29,100 --> 00:54:31,900
I can see the tank!

1101
00:54:33,910 --> 00:54:35,910
Can I fire? Fire!

1102
00:54:35,910 --> 00:54:38,700
From here—

1103
00:54:38,700 --> 00:54:42,510
Where, where, where?! Where do I shoot it from?!

1104
00:54:42,510 --> 00:54:43,310
North!

1105
00:54:43,310 --> 00:54:46,110
Wait, Polka might be closer.

1106
00:54:46,110 --> 00:54:47,110
Ow, ow!

1107
00:54:47,110 --> 00:54:51,280
You're pretty far out there — are you okay?

1108
00:54:51,280 --> 00:54:53,280
No! Visual, visual, visual!

1109
00:54:53,280 --> 00:54:54,280
Nice, nice!

1110
00:54:54,280 --> 00:54:55,280
For now—

1111
00:54:55,280 --> 00:54:56,280
Shoot from here!

1112
00:54:56,280 --> 00:54:57,280
I fired some shots!

1113
00:54:57,280 --> 00:54:58,900
Good!

1114
00:54:58,900 --> 00:55:01,380
Whoa!

1115
00:55:01,380 --> 00:55:03,380
No no no no — crab! Crab! Crab! Crab!

1116
00:55:03,380 --> 00:55:05,760
I forgot to crab walk! Crab! Scary, scary!

1117
00:55:05,760 --> 00:55:08,780
Crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab!

1118
00:55:08,780 --> 00:55:11,460
It's got a ton of aggro on you!

1119
00:55:11,460 --> 00:55:14,620
It's like firing from both sides right now.

1120
00:55:14,620 --> 00:55:18,160
The aggro's on Kanata, so Polka can shoot freely!

1121
00:55:18,160 --> 00:55:19,620
Oh, I see, probably.

1122
00:55:19,620 --> 00:55:20,980
The aggro's on me right now.

1123
00:55:20,980 --> 00:55:23,260
Crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab!

1124
00:55:23,260 --> 00:55:26,560
I can't see it from here — where's the tank?

1125
00:55:26,560 --> 00:55:33,110
Huh? Over there?

1126
00:55:32,910 --> 00:55:34,910
Crab crab crab crab crab crab crab crab crab crab!

1127
00:55:34,910 --> 00:55:35,910
Surely it won't walk over here, right?

1128
00:55:35,910 --> 00:55:38,910
Crab crab crab crab crab crab crab!

1129
00:55:38,910 --> 00:55:41,910
After firing that many shots, even the tank must have a cooldown, right?

1130
00:55:41,910 --> 00:55:43,910
Nope, it doesn't!

1131
00:55:43,910 --> 00:55:45,910
It's right in front of me!

1132
00:55:46,020 --> 00:55:47,910
Polka?

1133
00:55:47,910 --> 00:55:48,910
It was right in front of me!

1134
00:55:48,910 --> 00:55:49,910
Are you shooting?

1135
00:55:49,910 --> 00:55:50,910
Yeah, I'm shooting, I'm shooting!

1136
00:55:50,910 --> 00:55:52,910
You're just way too close to it!

1137
00:55:52,910 --> 00:55:54,910
Polka, where are you?! You're way too far forward!

1138
00:55:54,910 --> 00:55:56,910
You're gonna get killed!

1139
00:55:56,910 --> 00:55:58,910
Get back, further back!

1140
00:55:58,910 --> 00:55:59,910
Nooo!

1141
00:55:59,910 --> 00:56:01,910
Why are you even over there?!

1142
00:56:01,710 --> 00:56:05,740
Why did I die there?!

1143
00:56:05,740 --> 00:56:07,540
Come over here!

1144
00:56:07,540 --> 00:56:13,610
Oh, Polka's sleeping bag is here.

1145
00:56:13,610 --> 00:56:15,610
I died.

1146
00:56:15,610 --> 00:56:17,410
She's dead.

1147
00:56:17,410 --> 00:56:19,210
I died.

1148
00:56:19,210 --> 00:56:21,210
You can't be that close to it!

1149
00:56:21,210 --> 00:56:23,010
Come over here, this way!

1150
00:56:23,010 --> 00:56:25,010
And now she's dead.

1151
00:56:25,010 --> 00:56:26,810
Starting over from here again...

1152
00:56:26,810 --> 00:56:28,810
Oh no, it's so far away.

1153
00:56:28,810 --> 00:56:32,410
Now the fight against radiation begins.

1154
00:56:32,410 --> 00:56:41,170
Let me head back and drop off the suit first.

1155
00:56:41,170 --> 00:56:43,810
Or give me a sleeping bag.

1156
00:56:43,810 --> 00:56:47,410
You can give me the one from the camping car.

1157
00:56:47,410 --> 00:56:51,970
Hold on, let me head back to the camping car.

1158
00:56:51,970 --> 00:56:55,780
Hey, there's a cannonball flying over there!

1159
00:56:55,780 --> 00:57:00,580
Wait, the camping car was way further up ahead.

1160
00:57:00,580 --> 00:57:02,580
Ugh...

1161
00:57:02,580 --> 00:57:08,360
The camping car...

1162
00:57:08,360 --> 00:57:08,820
This is bad.

1163
00:57:08,820 --> 00:57:09,660
I knew it.

1164
00:57:09,660 --> 00:57:10,460
Whoa!

1165
00:57:10,460 --> 00:57:11,460
Ow ow ow ow!

1166
00:57:11,460 --> 00:57:12,460
I'm getting shot, I'm getting shot!

1167
00:57:12,460 --> 00:57:14,260
Practice and the real thing with Polka here

1168
00:57:14,260 --> 00:57:16,260
are just completely different.

1169
00:57:16,260 --> 00:57:18,060
It's so intense!

1170
00:57:18,060 --> 00:57:21,940
Next time, stay a good bit further —

1171
00:57:21,940 --> 00:57:23,940
like 150 meters —

1172
00:57:23,940 --> 00:57:25,790
away from it.

1173
00:57:25,790 --> 00:57:27,740
It's so intense!

1174
00:57:27,740 --> 00:57:29,540
Polka right now

1175
00:57:29,540 --> 00:57:31,540
is getting stressed out by boar sounds too.

1176
00:57:31,540 --> 00:57:34,340
Wait, can I just hand the sleeping bag to a friend?

1177
00:57:34,340 --> 00:57:36,340
Yeah, yeah, exactly!

1178
00:57:36,340 --> 00:57:38,340
Oh, an airdrop!

1179
00:57:38,340 --> 00:57:40,080
Thank you!

1180
00:57:40,080 --> 00:57:41,940
Let me put one suit back too.

1181
00:57:41,940 --> 00:57:42,940
Here.

1182
00:57:42,940 --> 00:57:44,910
There should be a Hazard Suit here...

1183
00:57:44,910 --> 00:57:46,700
there isn't one.

1184
00:57:46,700 --> 00:57:48,540
Um...

1185
00:57:48,540 --> 00:57:52,770
Can we go from here?

1186
00:57:52,770 --> 00:57:54,770
Hmm...

1187
00:57:54,770 --> 00:57:57,370
Oh, right.

1188
00:57:57,370 --> 00:57:59,030
Should I move back since it's dangerous here?

1189
00:57:59,030 --> 00:58:00,770
Wait, what do I do? Respawn?

1190
00:58:00,770 --> 00:58:01,750
Wh-what was it again?

1191
00:58:01,750 --> 00:58:06,210
Do I just... lie down here? Is that it?

1192
00:58:06,210 --> 00:58:08,410
I can't move from here.

1193
00:58:08,410 --> 00:58:12,570
Do I just... die here? What am I supposed to do?

1194
00:58:12,570 --> 00:58:14,890
I'm so confused.

1195
00:58:14,890 --> 00:58:16,550
Do I just respawn?

1196
00:58:16,550 --> 00:58:19,730
Okay.

1197
00:58:19,730 --> 00:58:22,610
I'll move a good distance away.

1198
00:58:22,610 --> 00:58:25,190
This car is actually pretty close to the tank.

1199
00:58:25,190 --> 00:58:30,400
That's what threw me off.

1200
00:58:30,400 --> 00:58:35,160
I completely misjudged how close the tank was.

1201
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:38,100
How about around here? Wait—

1202
00:58:38,100 --> 00:58:39,460
There it is!

1203
00:58:39,460 --> 00:58:40,660
Got it.

1204
00:58:40,660 --> 00:58:43,160
Right here.

1205
00:58:43,160 --> 00:58:44,900
How's this?

1206
00:58:44,900 --> 00:58:49,170
Okay, I'm heading out for a sec.

1207
00:58:49,170 --> 00:58:51,970


1208
00:58:51,970 --> 00:58:53,510
Where's the spawn point?

1209
00:58:53,510 --> 00:58:56,110
It'll spawn right there.

1210
00:58:56,110 --> 00:58:56,870
Let's go!

1211
00:58:56,870 --> 00:58:58,470
I ended up way farther away though.

1212
00:58:58,470 --> 00:58:59,510
Hello there.

1213
00:58:59,510 --> 00:59:00,410
I'm far away.

1214
00:59:00,410 --> 00:59:02,610


1215
00:59:02,610 --> 00:59:05,370
I went up to that little hill.

1216
00:59:05,370 --> 00:59:05,950
Taking damage.

1217
00:59:05,950 --> 00:59:07,270


1218
00:59:07,270 --> 00:59:07,870


1219
00:59:07,870 --> 00:59:10,290
The little hill.

1220
00:59:10,290 --> 00:59:12,810
There should be a Hazard Suit there too.

1221
00:59:12,810 --> 00:59:16,010
Thank you.

1222
00:59:16,010 --> 00:59:17,010
Una.

1223
00:59:17,010 --> 00:59:18,790
It's Una.

1224
00:59:18,790 --> 00:59:21,890
A sleeping bag... but in overseas servers, you can't place them on vehicles.

1225
00:59:21,890 --> 00:59:22,690
Oh right, food.

1226
00:59:22,690 --> 00:59:23,690
Definitely!

1227
00:59:23,690 --> 00:59:26,990
Oh, there's pumpkins!

1228
00:59:26,990 --> 00:59:28,790
Give me some pumpkins.

1229
00:59:28,790 --> 00:59:31,090
Pumpkins coming in.

1230
00:59:31,090 --> 00:59:33,610
Thanks!

1231
00:59:33,610 --> 00:59:37,010
Earlier...

1232
00:59:37,010 --> 00:59:39,710
A little further back here should be fine.

1233
00:59:39,710 --> 00:59:43,610
Is this it? I feel like I'm not hitting it at all.

1234
00:59:43,610 --> 00:59:45,610
Yeah, you're not... you're not hitting it, it's too far.

1235
00:59:45,610 --> 00:59:49,440
Right?

1236
00:59:49,540 --> 00:59:50,800
Okay.

1237
00:59:50,800 --> 00:59:53,220
But at least the tank spawned, so that's good.

1238
00:59:53,220 --> 00:59:54,460
Yeah, that's good.

1239
00:59:54,460 --> 00:59:56,440
Good thing we made a reservation.

1240
00:59:56,440 --> 01:00:00,440
Turns out it really was a tank you can't get without a reservation.

1241
01:00:00,440 --> 01:00:03,500
It showed up out of nowhere though.

1242
01:00:03,500 --> 01:00:05,540
True.

1243
01:00:05,540 --> 01:00:07,840
I still want some kind of heads-up that it's coming.

1244
01:00:07,840 --> 01:00:16,680
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho!

1245
01:00:16,680 --> 01:00:23,060
Like with the tank, ideally I'd want something like the heli — showing where it is on the map right now.

1246
01:00:23,060 --> 01:00:25,460
Yeah, there's nothing like that.

1247
01:00:25,460 --> 01:00:28,460
Crab walk, crab walk, crab walk, crab walk!

1248
01:00:28,460 --> 01:00:31,010
Right, and around here—

1249
01:00:31,010 --> 01:00:31,780
Oh, I can hear it.

1250
01:00:31,780 --> 01:00:39,080
Like, shoot from the front here and then fall back.

1251
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:40,680
Yeah I can hear it, it's coming from inside.

1252
01:00:40,680 --> 01:00:43,000
Cut across lanes.

1253
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:45,200
Cut across lanes, right, that's it.

1254
01:00:45,200 --> 01:00:47,000
Oh yeah, that was from Matsuri-chan.

1255
01:00:47,000 --> 01:00:49,000
I was pushing a bit too far forward there.

1256
01:00:49,000 --> 01:00:50,000
Around here.

1257
01:00:50,000 --> 01:00:52,000
It's super loud around here, isn't it?

1258
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:53,000
Yeah it is.

1259
01:00:53,000 --> 01:00:55,800
It's here! Visual! Visual, visual!

1260
01:00:55,800 --> 01:00:57,600
Did you shoot?

1261
01:00:57,600 --> 01:00:59,330
I missed.

1262
01:00:59,330 --> 01:01:00,200
It went right past.

1263
01:01:00,200 --> 01:01:03,660
Visual confirmed!

1264
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:05,660
What do you mean, visual?!

1265
01:01:05,660 --> 01:01:08,460
I mean I can actually see it!

1266
01:01:08,460 --> 01:01:11,420
Polka?

1267
01:01:11,420 --> 01:01:12,420
I'm running away.

1268
01:01:13,220 --> 01:01:14,220
I can't, it's scary!

1269
01:01:14,220 --> 01:01:15,180
Go down.

1270
01:01:15,180 --> 01:01:16,520
Down?

1271
01:01:16,520 --> 01:01:19,350
Over here, over here!

1272
01:01:19,350 --> 01:01:22,950
Wait, where are you, Polka?

1273
01:01:22,950 --> 01:01:24,750
Down here, right here, inside this.

1274
01:01:24,750 --> 01:01:31,330
Okay okay okay okay!

1275
01:01:31,330 --> 01:01:33,330
I'm in here.

1276
01:01:33,330 --> 01:01:34,330
There you are!

1277
01:01:34,330 --> 01:01:39,040
This is the route Azuki taught us yesterday.

1278
01:01:39,040 --> 01:01:41,650
Can the tank come in here?

1279
01:01:41,650 --> 01:01:43,640
It can't come in, so we hide here.

1280
01:01:43,640 --> 01:01:47,600
The tank's out there.

1281
01:01:48,100 --> 01:01:49,990
It's there.

1282
01:01:49,990 --> 01:01:52,450
Are the NPCs getting rowdy too?

1283
01:01:52,450 --> 01:01:57,790
They're not rowdy, but if you peek out, they're right there.

1284
01:01:57,790 --> 01:01:59,610
You're right.

1285
01:01:59,610 --> 01:02:04,050
I've never been over this way.

1286
01:02:04,050 --> 01:02:07,170
They're waiting for us to come out.

1287
01:02:07,170 --> 01:02:10,130
Wait, aren't we trapped like rats in a bag?

1288
01:02:10,130 --> 01:02:13,840
From the other side—

1289
01:02:13,840 --> 01:02:15,320
Oh, this—

1290
01:02:15,320 --> 01:02:17,240
Oh wait, NPCs are coming!

1291
01:02:17,240 --> 01:02:20,040
Oh, is this okay? I don't have a gun! Of all things—

1292
01:02:20,040 --> 01:02:21,840
Oh, they're here.

1293
01:02:21,840 --> 01:02:24,640
I don't have a gun of all things — Kanatan, help!

1294
01:02:24,640 --> 01:02:27,440
Apparently if the NPCs break through, you should retreat for now.

1295
01:02:27,440 --> 01:02:28,440
Got it.

1296
01:02:28,440 --> 01:02:30,240
But retreat to where?

1297
01:02:30,240 --> 01:02:33,040
Hey Kanatan, this map—

1298
01:02:33,040 --> 01:02:35,040
Oh, I think Pol has the tank's aggro now.

1299
01:02:35,040 --> 01:02:39,970
Is it that way? Should I come out from Pol's side?

1300
01:02:39,970 --> 01:02:47,920
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

1301
01:02:49,440 --> 01:02:52,440
It's probably around NE.

1302
01:02:52,440 --> 01:02:54,240
Oh, it's gone back to neutral.

1303
01:02:54,240 --> 01:02:56,040
Where did the tank go?

1304
01:02:56,040 --> 01:02:57,870
The tank went that way too.

1305
01:02:57,870 --> 01:03:00,840
It's around NE 60 direction.

1306
01:03:00,840 --> 01:03:02,640
NE 60, copy.

1307
01:03:02,640 --> 01:03:03,440
That's far.

1308
01:03:03,440 --> 01:03:06,240
Okay, let's aim from here.

1309
01:03:06,240 --> 01:03:10,190
Is it not hitting?

1310
01:03:16,670 --> 01:03:20,910
The tank went back to its original position.

1311
01:03:20,910 --> 01:03:24,780
It went back in front of the room.

1312
01:03:24,780 --> 01:03:26,630
I see.

1313
01:03:26,630 --> 01:03:29,830
Where's its original position?

1314
01:03:29,830 --> 01:03:32,630
We need to go recover Polka's body.

1315
01:03:32,630 --> 01:03:34,430
Where the sleeping bag spawns.

1316
01:03:34,430 --> 01:03:38,880
Oh, Pol's body — oh, it's at that little hill.

1317
01:03:38,880 --> 01:03:40,880
Oh right, I don't remember — where was it again?

1318
01:03:40,880 --> 01:03:42,680
It's over there.

1319
01:03:42,680 --> 01:03:44,480
The little hill.

1320
01:03:44,480 --> 01:03:46,480
The little hill, huh — that's a bit scary.

1321
01:03:46,480 --> 01:03:50,280
Yeah, the tank's—

1322
01:03:52,080 --> 01:03:54,080
It was pretty close, wasn't it.

1323
01:03:54,080 --> 01:03:56,280
Around the M8 marker.

1324
01:03:56,280 --> 01:03:57,920
But we could probably make it now, right?

1325
01:03:57,920 --> 01:04:00,360
Which way?

1326
01:04:00,360 --> 01:04:02,220
It's here, right? NE 40.

1327
01:04:02,220 --> 01:04:03,400
Around this room.

1328
01:04:03,400 --> 01:04:08,020
Pol's sleeping bag is around here, right?

1329
01:04:08,020 --> 01:04:08,820
Hm?

1330
01:04:08,820 --> 01:04:11,600
Wasn't it around here?

1331
01:04:11,600 --> 01:04:12,600
There it is, there it is!

1332
01:04:12,600 --> 01:04:13,600
Oh, thanks!

1333
01:04:13,600 --> 01:04:15,000
This is it, this is it!

1334
01:04:15,000 --> 01:04:16,800
Without this sleeping bag, we'd be done for.

1335
01:04:16,800 --> 01:04:17,800
We can't get back up without it.

1336
01:04:21,470 --> 01:04:27,950
I went too far forward before, so I'll push back — I can't even hear the tank.

1337
01:04:27,950 --> 01:04:37,010
Silence. It's not around here. Once we recover, let's fall back — okay.

1338
01:04:37,010 --> 01:04:41,990
The tank's probably inside the sensor range, patrolling.

1339
01:04:41,990 --> 01:04:44,820
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

1340
01:04:44,820 --> 01:04:50,200
It's in there — Kanatan!

1341
01:04:50,560 --> 01:04:52,460
I was hoping it'd come this way.

1342
01:04:52,460 --> 01:04:53,420
Lure it?

1343
01:04:53,420 --> 01:04:55,040
With a guided missile?

1344
01:04:55,040 --> 01:04:56,040
Yeah.

1345
01:04:56,040 --> 01:05:02,450
It's there!

1346
01:05:02,450 --> 01:05:08,120
Where?

1347
01:05:08,120 --> 01:05:14,670
It's there but it looks like it might hit a wall.

1348
01:05:14,670 --> 01:05:19,870
Which direction?

1349
01:05:19,870 --> 01:05:21,730
Hmm, where is it...

1350
01:05:21,730 --> 01:05:25,780
I can hear it but I can't see it.

1351
01:05:25,780 --> 01:05:27,220
Oh, there it is!

1352
01:05:27,220 --> 01:05:28,780
Around N 20.

1353
01:05:28,920 --> 01:05:30,080
N 20, copy.

1354
01:05:30,080 --> 01:05:32,140
It's shifted to N 30 and to the right.

1355
01:05:32,140 --> 01:05:33,140
It's in the shadows.

1356
01:05:33,140 --> 01:05:40,800
I lost sight of the tank!

1357
01:05:40,800 --> 01:05:45,320
Yesterday too, the tank took a while to come out, right?

1358
01:05:45,320 --> 01:05:47,360
Didn't someone say they trapped it somehow?

1359
01:05:47,360 --> 01:05:49,740
Sounds like there was a spot where it got stuck.

1360
01:05:49,740 --> 01:05:53,740
It got stuck on the turret and they just kept shooting it.

1361
01:05:53,740 --> 01:05:57,540
Was there black smoke? Did we hit it?

1362
01:05:57,540 --> 01:05:58,220
Excellent!

1363
01:05:59,120 --> 01:06:00,520
Oh, there it is, there it is!

1364
01:06:00,520 --> 01:06:04,720
It's around NE50, 40—

1365
01:06:04,720 --> 01:06:06,920
There it is!

1366
01:06:06,920 --> 01:06:10,210
Come over here!

1367
01:06:10,210 --> 01:06:11,910
It's coming!

1368
01:06:11,910 --> 01:06:14,510
It's coming, it's coming!

1369
01:06:14,510 --> 01:06:16,710
Does a hit sound different somehow?

1370
01:06:16,710 --> 01:06:18,210
Like a kind of "thwump" sound.

1371
01:06:18,210 --> 01:06:18,910
Huh?!

1372
01:06:18,910 --> 01:06:19,710
I want to hear that sound.

1373
01:06:19,710 --> 01:06:20,310
Oh ho!

1374
01:06:20,310 --> 01:06:29,600
Babababababa!

1375
01:06:29,600 --> 01:06:30,400
There it is!

1376
01:06:30,400 --> 01:06:32,000
Whoa!

1377
01:06:32,000 --> 01:06:33,700
I wanna hear that sound!

1378
01:06:33,700 --> 01:06:35,860
I wanna hear you cry!

1379
01:06:35,860 --> 01:06:38,160
That one went wide.

1380
01:06:38,160 --> 01:06:42,950
Is this sound no good?

1381
01:06:42,950 --> 01:06:45,250
It sounds like a magic spell.

1382
01:06:45,250 --> 01:06:46,250
It's coming this way!

1383
01:06:46,250 --> 01:06:51,860
Yeaaah~

1384
01:06:51,860 --> 01:06:53,500
Not at all.

1385
01:06:54,520 --> 01:07:00,080
Aaaah my aim is absolute garbage!

1386
01:07:00,080 --> 01:07:02,760


1387
01:07:02,760 --> 01:07:05,240
Where is it right now?

1388
01:07:05,240 --> 01:07:06,540
N, N10.

1389
01:07:06,540 --> 01:07:09,640
N3, 350.

1390
01:07:09,640 --> 01:07:13,970
Got it.

1391
01:07:13,970 --> 01:07:18,390
Luna's getting hit by the turret.

1392
01:07:18,390 --> 01:07:19,330
Over there—

1393
01:07:19,330 --> 01:07:21,410
Around N10.

1394
01:07:21,410 --> 01:07:23,110
It went inside, it went inside!

1395
01:07:23,110 --> 01:07:28,940
Oh no, oh no.

1396
01:07:28,940 --> 01:07:29,940
Whoa!

1397
01:07:29,940 --> 01:07:35,540
If I don't leave this spot, it's rough coming from this side.

1398
01:07:35,540 --> 01:07:39,060
I can't get a clear angle from here either.

1399
01:07:39,060 --> 01:07:40,260
Where is it?

1400
01:07:40,260 --> 01:07:43,900
I wonder if it'll get stuck.

1401
01:07:43,900 --> 01:07:47,980
Okay, fall back.

1402
01:07:47,980 --> 01:07:51,740
I can't see it!

1403
01:07:51,740 --> 01:07:53,300
Enemy soldiers.

1404
01:07:53,300 --> 01:07:59,620
None here.

1405
01:07:59,620 --> 01:08:02,380
Did it go on patrol somewhere again?

1406
01:08:03,140 --> 01:08:06,620
Hmm?

1407
01:08:06,620 --> 01:08:07,620
It's not here.

1408
01:08:07,620 --> 01:08:08,620
It's not here.

1409
01:08:08,620 --> 01:08:09,620
It wandered off again.

1410
01:08:09,620 --> 01:08:11,420
Come on out!

1411
01:08:11,420 --> 01:08:13,220
Oh wait, it's there.

1412
01:08:13,220 --> 01:08:14,220
Around N40.

1413
01:08:14,220 --> 01:08:17,130
There it is, there it is.

1414
01:08:17,130 --> 01:08:19,130
I can see its eye thing.

1415
01:08:19,130 --> 01:08:19,930
Nice.

1416
01:08:19,930 --> 01:08:23,730
But it's a bit too far to fire a missile.

1417
01:08:23,730 --> 01:08:25,530
Really?

1418
01:08:25,530 --> 01:08:28,330
I can only see the top of it.

1419
01:08:28,330 --> 01:08:32,470
It's hiding!

1420
01:08:32,470 --> 01:08:34,470
So it's hiding too?

1421
01:08:34,470 --> 01:08:37,260
Oh, you're right!

1422
01:08:37,260 --> 01:08:39,070
I can see its eye!

1423
01:08:39,070 --> 01:08:40,870
Let's just shoot at it for now.

1424
01:08:40,870 --> 01:08:43,870
There are like a ton of airdrops coming down.

1425
01:08:43,870 --> 01:08:49,050
Hey, is it stuck again? Look at that.

1426
01:08:49,050 --> 01:08:50,850
Oh, then let's just trap it there!

1427
01:08:50,850 --> 01:08:55,570
I'm not sure, but even when it's stuck it still attacks.

1428
01:08:55,570 --> 01:08:56,450
Really?

1429
01:08:56,450 --> 01:08:59,250
We just have to crab-walk to dodge.

1430
01:09:02,750 --> 01:09:08,070
You're right, it's trying to move.

1431
01:09:08,070 --> 01:09:11,870
Isn't this our chance?

1432
01:09:11,870 --> 01:09:15,470
Hit it. In the match.

1433
01:09:15,470 --> 01:09:18,270
Oh, so close! A little too high.

1434
01:09:18,270 --> 01:09:24,400
This is hard.

1435
01:09:24,400 --> 01:09:27,200
Hit!

1436
01:09:27,200 --> 01:09:30,000
If it's the same as before—

1437
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:32,800
That thing is seriously stuck.

1438
01:09:32,800 --> 01:09:34,680
Someone's probably shooting from below.

1439
01:09:34,680 --> 01:09:36,700
Oh, this totally isn't working.

1440
01:09:36,700 --> 01:09:42,170
Yeah, this isn't right.

1441
01:09:42,170 --> 01:09:45,750
Yeah, it's really hard to hit from here.

1442
01:09:45,750 --> 01:09:47,550
Ah, too high.

1443
01:09:47,550 --> 01:09:48,550
Wait, where was it again?

1444
01:09:48,550 --> 01:09:49,550
Too high.

1445
01:09:49,550 --> 01:09:51,190
Like a guided missile...

1446
01:09:51,190 --> 01:09:53,170
It looks like just a tiny bit above.

1447
01:09:53,170 --> 01:09:54,850
Just a tiny bit higher, is that right?

1448
01:09:54,850 --> 01:09:58,600
Oh no, oh no no no!

1449
01:09:58,600 --> 01:09:59,780
It's heading toward Luna!

1450
01:09:59,780 --> 01:10:06,400
Oh, that's looking pretty good!

1451
01:10:06,400 --> 01:10:08,400
It's already broken line of sight.

1452
01:10:08,400 --> 01:10:14,720


1453
01:10:14,720 --> 01:10:21,840
Did that one hit?

1454
01:10:21,840 --> 01:10:23,640
Nice, nice — it's on fire!

1455
01:10:23,640 --> 01:10:27,500
It's burning!

1456
01:10:27,500 --> 01:10:30,900
Still alive though.

1457
01:10:30,900 --> 01:10:38,290
Luna's got full aggro, so that's a big help.

1458
01:10:38,290 --> 01:10:40,090
Ow!

1459
01:10:40,090 --> 01:10:41,490
Okay, for now—

1460
01:10:41,490 --> 01:10:45,560
I can't even see it anymore, it's all on fire.

1461
01:10:50,540 --> 01:10:52,540
Alright, let's line up another shot.

1462
01:10:52,540 --> 01:10:56,680
Getting closer is scary though.

1463
01:10:56,680 --> 01:10:59,360
Getting closer is a bad idea.

1464
01:10:59,360 --> 01:11:04,800
Wait, is it hitting that weird white wall? Is it okay?

1465
01:11:04,800 --> 01:11:08,130
Did that land?

1466
01:11:08,130 --> 01:11:16,320
The rockets keep hitting that white wall, so shooting from this side would be better — but shells are coming, so I need to crab-walk to dodge.

1467
01:11:17,880 --> 01:11:20,880
Kanatan, where are you~?

1468
01:11:20,880 --> 01:11:26,630
That was a bit off.

1469
01:11:26,630 --> 01:11:29,290
Wait, is that a heli — heli — helicopter coming?

1470
01:11:29,290 --> 01:11:30,530
No it's not.

1471
01:11:30,530 --> 01:11:31,520
That thing—

1472
01:11:31,520 --> 01:11:34,250
Up ahead—

1473
01:11:34,250 --> 01:11:39,250
Wait, that thing is clearly looking right at us.

1474
01:11:39,250 --> 01:11:45,270
Hold on! I haven't done anything wrong! Stop it!

1475
01:11:45,270 --> 01:11:51,970
I'm a law-abiding citizen! It's fine, I'm just nearby!

1476
01:11:51,970 --> 01:11:58,990
Ow! Ow! Ow! I didn't do anything!

1477
01:11:58,990 --> 01:12:02,720
Why?!

1478
01:12:03,220 --> 01:12:08,380
Ow ow ow ow ow! That's awful!

1479
01:12:08,380 --> 01:12:12,360
Why?! This is too much!

1480
01:12:12,360 --> 01:12:17,160
Indiscriminate fire! What is the tank even doing?!

1481
01:12:17,160 --> 01:12:24,460
Like, what if the tank somehow recovers its health after this—

1482
01:12:24,460 --> 01:12:29,740
I dunno, I don't think it actually heals.

1483
01:12:29,740 --> 01:12:35,500
The heli's here too — it's backup! Ow! Get out of here!

1484
01:12:35,500 --> 01:12:39,000
How many shots does it take to bring down the heli? Hahaha!

1485
01:12:39,000 --> 01:12:45,420
It's the big one! And there's this too! No way, no way! We're gonna die!

1486
01:12:45,420 --> 01:12:51,190
What is that thing?!

1487
01:12:51,190 --> 01:12:59,970
Why do we always get such a warm welcome when we show up? Though it's kind of nice in a way.

1488
01:13:01,270 --> 01:13:03,070
Is it still there?

1489
01:13:03,070 --> 01:13:05,070
Still there, still there — yeah it's definitely still there, like—

1490
01:13:05,070 --> 01:13:06,870
That one's just wandering around too.

1491
01:13:06,870 --> 01:13:08,870
Why is it hanging around here?

1492
01:13:08,870 --> 01:13:10,870
This one's on patrol too.

1493
01:13:10,870 --> 01:13:12,670
Hey—!

1494
01:13:12,670 --> 01:13:14,610
Go home, go home!

1495
01:13:14,610 --> 01:13:16,270
Polka—

1496
01:13:16,270 --> 01:13:18,270
It's not in my inventory, okay?

1497
01:13:18,270 --> 01:13:20,270
I don't have any guns in here!

1498
01:13:20,270 --> 01:13:22,070
Don't look at me.

1499
01:13:22,070 --> 01:13:24,070
How does it even know I have guns in my inventory?

1500
01:13:24,070 --> 01:13:25,870
That makes no sense.

1501
01:13:25,870 --> 01:13:27,870
It's just circling around!

1502
01:13:27,870 --> 01:13:33,070
Well, we've been spotted now, so whatever.

1503
01:13:33,070 --> 01:13:35,690
Akai-san can take it down in four shots.

1504
01:13:35,690 --> 01:13:37,250
I'm talking about Akai-san.

1505
01:13:37,250 --> 01:13:38,650
She can do it in four shots?

1506
01:13:38,650 --> 01:13:39,270
Four shots.

1507
01:13:39,270 --> 01:13:41,610
Its movement pattern changed a lot.

1508
01:13:41,610 --> 01:13:47,770
Could you please stop with the anti-air fire?

1509
01:13:47,770 --> 01:13:49,190
This is seriously bad.

1510
01:13:49,190 --> 01:13:52,210
Getting attacked from both Riku and Kuu—

1511
01:13:52,210 --> 01:13:53,130
It moved away.

1512
01:13:53,130 --> 01:13:56,910
I want to wait just a little longer, but—

1513
01:13:56,910 --> 01:13:58,730
Goodbye.

1514
01:13:58,730 --> 01:13:59,630
Go home.

1515
01:13:59,630 --> 01:14:02,910
Is it leaving?

1516
01:14:02,910 --> 01:14:04,750
Yeah, it's leaving, it's leaving — it's really leaving right now!

1517
01:14:04,750 --> 01:14:05,330
It's gone, it's gone!

1518
01:14:05,330 --> 01:14:07,790
And now it's gonna be nighttime.

1519
01:14:07,790 --> 01:14:11,030
We were so close too.

1520
01:14:11,030 --> 01:14:13,430
Goodbye.

1521
01:14:13,430 --> 01:14:14,490
Goodbye.

1522
01:14:14,490 --> 01:14:16,310
Please don't come back for a while.

1523
01:14:16,310 --> 01:14:20,370
What is even going on?

1524
01:14:20,370 --> 01:14:23,250
Things were going so well too.

1525
01:14:23,250 --> 01:14:27,350
They overheat when they get hit too much.

1526
01:14:27,350 --> 01:14:29,310
I had no idea.

1527
01:14:29,310 --> 01:14:30,390
It's still stuck.

1528
01:14:30,390 --> 01:14:35,900
Yeah, it's stuck.

1529
01:14:35,900 --> 01:14:38,780
Please stay stuck, I'm begging you.

1530
01:14:38,780 --> 01:14:42,850
Nice!

1531
01:14:42,850 --> 01:14:47,310
I can hear the hits landing.

1532
01:14:47,310 --> 01:14:48,390
A night battle, Princess?

1533
01:14:48,390 --> 01:14:49,290
Oh, it's already past dawn.

1534
01:14:49,290 --> 01:14:52,370
No, it should be getting dark again soon.

1535
01:14:52,370 --> 01:14:52,970
What?

1536
01:14:52,970 --> 01:14:56,170
Oh, we got it!

1537
01:14:56,170 --> 01:14:56,970
Wait, really?

1538
01:14:56,970 --> 01:14:59,770
We did it, Princess! We're doing it!

1539
01:14:59,770 --> 01:15:00,770
Did we get it?

1540
01:15:00,770 --> 01:15:01,570
It's over! It's done!

1541
01:15:01,570 --> 01:15:02,570
It's finally over~

1542
01:15:02,570 --> 01:15:04,570
The battle is over!

1543
01:15:04,570 --> 01:15:07,770
The battle is done~

1544
01:15:07,770 --> 01:15:10,570
The battle is over!

1545
01:15:10,570 --> 01:15:14,370
While Polka was struggling, Kanata landed all the shots.

1546
01:15:14,370 --> 01:15:18,170
Popo was shooting too!

1547
01:15:18,170 --> 01:15:20,170
Popo was shooting too~

1548
01:15:20,170 --> 01:15:22,970
I was hitting it, I was hitting it~

1549
01:15:22,970 --> 01:15:24,970
It's on fire!

1550
01:15:24,970 --> 01:15:26,970
Getting it stuck is so powerful.

1551
01:15:26,970 --> 01:15:30,570
Though we lost to the stuck mechanic like 3 times ourselves.

1552
01:15:30,570 --> 01:15:33,420
This spot really does get things stuck.

1553
01:15:33,420 --> 01:15:36,170
It's burning nicely.

1554
01:15:36,170 --> 01:15:37,970
It's hot, it's hot!

1555
01:15:37,970 --> 01:15:41,970
Once the fire dies down, three crates should appear and we can loot them.

1556
01:15:41,970 --> 01:15:44,970
Right, you can't go near it while it's still on fire.

1557
01:15:44,970 --> 01:15:49,520
Hot hot hot hot hot!

1558
01:15:49,520 --> 01:15:52,520
It burned, it burned — it burned yesterday too.

1559
01:15:52,520 --> 01:15:53,520
Yeah, like...

1560
01:15:53,520 --> 01:15:56,750
It just draws you in.

1561
01:15:56,750 --> 01:15:57,750
We did it!

1562
01:15:57,750 --> 01:15:59,550
Congratulations!

1563
01:15:59,550 --> 01:16:01,350
We did it!

1564
01:16:01,350 --> 01:16:05,150
And it showing up on the map for everyone — that feels so good.

1565
01:16:05,150 --> 01:16:08,550
Oh, you're right!

1566
01:16:08,550 --> 01:16:09,550
For everyone to see.

1567
01:16:09,550 --> 01:16:12,350
That we pulled it off.

1568
01:16:12,350 --> 01:16:14,150
We did it!

1569
01:16:14,150 --> 01:16:16,950
Wooo!

1570
01:16:17,940 --> 01:16:21,710
A commemorative photo? Oh, I forgot to bring a camera.

1571
01:16:21,710 --> 01:16:22,550
Screenshot, screenshot!

1572
01:16:22,550 --> 01:16:26,290
No camera.

1573
01:16:26,290 --> 01:16:28,270
Phew~

1574
01:16:28,270 --> 01:16:30,890
Yesterday's practice...

1575
01:16:30,890 --> 01:16:31,890
...really paid off.

1576
01:16:31,890 --> 01:16:33,890
It really did.

1577
01:16:33,890 --> 01:16:42,190
Without Azuki's training yesterday, it would've been really hard to teach Polka too.

1578
01:16:42,190 --> 01:16:46,090
For sure, we both would've gotten completely wrecked.

1579
01:16:46,090 --> 01:16:49,890
It was seriously rough.

1580
01:16:49,890 --> 01:16:55,410
So this is the end of our battle, huh.

1581
01:16:55,410 --> 01:16:58,240
Yeah, finally.

1582
01:16:58,240 --> 01:17:02,090
Finally, no more regrets...

1583
01:17:02,090 --> 01:17:03,890
Right?

1584
01:17:03,890 --> 01:17:05,690
Yeah, none.

1585
01:17:05,690 --> 01:17:06,690
Is there anything left?

1586
01:17:08,490 --> 01:17:11,090
I feel like we really gave it our all.

1587
01:17:11,090 --> 01:17:13,610
We really did.

1588
01:17:13,610 --> 01:17:16,130
We did it!

1589
01:17:16,130 --> 01:17:20,850
What about the helicopter? The heli is insane, that thing is scary.

1590
01:17:20,850 --> 01:17:23,230
The helicopter though...

1591
01:17:23,230 --> 01:17:26,390
But if you hit it enough it goes down, right? That's impressive too.

1592
01:17:26,390 --> 01:17:29,300
We'd die from the missiles too though.

1593
01:17:29,300 --> 01:17:34,890
Yeah, you can't exactly crab-walk to dodge a helicopter.

1594
01:17:34,890 --> 01:17:36,890
Crab-walking doesn't seem like it'd work, does it?

1595
01:17:36,890 --> 01:17:38,890
Crab-walking is the least of your worries with a helicopter.

1596
01:17:38,890 --> 01:17:41,690
I don't even know how you're supposed to fight a helicopter.

1597
01:17:41,690 --> 01:17:50,110
Homing missiles.

1598
01:17:50,110 --> 01:17:51,710
I wonder...

1599
01:17:51,710 --> 01:17:53,710
Oh, there are homing ones?

1600
01:17:53,710 --> 01:17:55,710
Oh right, we had homing missiles back at base.

1601
01:17:55,710 --> 01:17:57,510
Yeah, yeah, we did!

1602
01:17:57,510 --> 01:17:59,510
I see.

1603
01:17:59,510 --> 01:18:02,310
The crab walk is impossible for me.

1604
01:18:02,310 --> 01:18:04,110
Yeah, the crab walk just isn't happening.

1605
01:18:04,110 --> 01:18:06,080
The mini-heli only takes 4 hits.

1606
01:18:06,080 --> 01:18:07,910
The one earlier was huge though.

1607
01:18:07,910 --> 01:18:13,850
Even with 4 rockets, it's flying around, so it'd be hard to hit.

1608
01:18:13,650 --> 01:18:14,650
Hmm...

1609
01:18:17,680 --> 01:18:19,970
Wh- wha- wha-

1610
01:18:19,970 --> 01:18:24,450
Oh! The box— hit it, hit it, hit it!

1611
01:18:24,450 --> 01:18:26,310
Come on, come on!

1612
01:18:26,310 --> 01:18:30,470
I can see the loot boxes, but every time I try to go touch them, they're still hot!

1613
01:18:32,790 --> 01:18:33,970
I can't resist!

1614
01:18:33,970 --> 01:18:35,530
Oh, I get it, I get it.

1615
01:18:35,530 --> 01:18:38,290
We just can't help opening boxes when we see them in Rust.

1616
01:18:38,290 --> 01:18:39,450
Right.

1617
01:18:39,450 --> 01:18:44,190
Like in real life, when you see a screw you just want to scrap it.

1618
01:18:44,190 --> 01:18:45,330
Was it a super ball?

1619
01:18:45,330 --> 01:18:46,650
Oh, what is that?

1620
01:18:46,650 --> 01:18:48,550
Oh, what is that?

1621
01:18:48,550 --> 01:18:52,360
It's a super ball!

1622
01:18:52,360 --> 01:18:54,600


1623
01:18:54,600 --> 01:18:56,640


1624
01:18:56,640 --> 01:18:58,200
It's still on fire.

1625
01:18:58,200 --> 01:19:01,440
I hope something good comes out of it.

1626
01:19:01,740 --> 01:19:03,260
What do you want from it?

1627
01:19:03,260 --> 01:19:04,340
The fire...

1628
01:19:04,340 --> 01:19:05,620
Oh.

1629
01:19:05,620 --> 01:19:07,760
It's dying down.

1630
01:19:07,760 --> 01:19:08,960
Hurry up and go out already!

1631
01:19:08,960 --> 01:19:09,860
Ugh, ugh, ugh...

1632
01:19:09,860 --> 01:19:15,100
Still burning strong.

1633
01:19:15,100 --> 01:19:19,370
Still going strong.

1634
01:19:19,370 --> 01:19:21,210
Still, still, still...

1635
01:19:21,210 --> 01:19:23,450
Maybe we should just dump water on it to cool it down.

1636
01:19:23,450 --> 01:19:26,330
I don't think dumping water on it actually cools it down.

1637
01:19:26,330 --> 01:19:27,850
The fire's dying down.

1638
01:19:27,850 --> 01:19:30,860
It's dying down?

1639
01:19:30,860 --> 01:19:33,640
I wonder what's inside~

1640
01:19:33,640 --> 01:19:35,740
I mean, Kanata, you know...

1641
01:19:35,740 --> 01:19:39,420
Hey, I really want the M249 to drop — that's been the dream!

1642
01:19:39,420 --> 01:19:40,560
Here we go!

1643
01:19:40,560 --> 01:19:43,420
This one's still hot though...

1644
01:19:43,420 --> 01:19:44,340
Oh, it's fine, it's fine!

1645
01:19:44,340 --> 01:19:45,340
It's okay already?

1646
01:19:45,340 --> 01:19:47,300
Alright, let's check the first one.

1647
01:19:47,300 --> 01:19:49,060
Here goes!

1648
01:19:49,060 --> 01:19:49,960
Here goes!

1649
01:19:49,960 --> 01:19:53,780
There's a PC in there, but...

1650
01:19:53,780 --> 01:19:56,880
Hmm, well...

1651
01:19:56,880 --> 01:19:58,590
Box number 2!

1652
01:19:58,590 --> 01:20:00,480
What's in box 2?

1653
01:20:00,480 --> 01:20:03,280
This one lying on its side.

1654
01:20:03,280 --> 01:20:03,780
Okay!

1655
01:20:03,780 --> 01:20:04,880
Okay!

1656
01:20:04,880 --> 01:20:05,980
Oh, what's this?!

1657
01:20:05,980 --> 01:20:09,920
It's here, Kanata!

1658
01:20:09,720 --> 01:20:10,720
No way!

1659
01:20:10,720 --> 01:20:12,480
Oh ho ho!

1660
01:20:12,720 --> 01:20:13,720
First time ever getting this!

1661
01:20:13,720 --> 01:20:14,720
What the heck?! This is insane!

1662
01:20:14,720 --> 01:20:16,720
Test fire it, test fire it!

1663
01:20:16,720 --> 01:20:19,720
Of all places, it actually dropped here!

1664
01:20:19,720 --> 01:20:20,720
Let's gooo!

1665
01:20:20,720 --> 01:20:26,720
All that hard work paid off!

1666
01:20:26,720 --> 01:20:27,720
Oh wow!

1667
01:20:28,410 --> 01:20:29,610
Let's open the other one too!

1668
01:20:29,610 --> 01:20:31,550
Yes!

1669
01:20:31,550 --> 01:20:32,550
Yay!

1670
01:20:32,550 --> 01:20:33,650
Which one is the other box?

1671
01:20:33,650 --> 01:20:34,450
Oh, this one!

1672
01:20:34,450 --> 01:20:35,050
Here!

1673
01:20:35,050 --> 01:20:35,850
Here!

1674
01:20:35,850 --> 01:20:38,970
More rockets coming out.

1675
01:20:38,970 --> 01:20:41,710
It's like the game really wants us to use rockets.

1676
01:20:41,710 --> 01:20:43,990
The M249 actually dropped!

1677
01:20:43,990 --> 01:20:46,830
Getting the M249 here is absolutely insane!

1678
01:20:46,830 --> 01:20:50,430
Of all things...

1679
01:20:50,430 --> 01:20:54,990
Guess we have no choice but to do something with it in the night session.

1680
01:20:54,990 --> 01:20:58,250
We have to do something with this.

1681
01:20:58,250 --> 01:21:02,970
Go ahead and shoot it, Luna!

1682
01:21:02,970 --> 01:21:09,770
Should I fire it? Should I? Come on, try shooting something! Should I? Don't shoot Polka though!

1683
01:21:09,770 --> 01:21:15,370
I wonder how much damage this does? We need a target or something.

1684
01:21:15,370 --> 01:21:19,170
Whoa! Whoaaa! The sound is different! Ohhh!

1685
01:21:19,170 --> 01:21:22,170
Oh, she's breaking that with a jackhammer! Amazing!

1686
01:21:22,170 --> 01:21:25,970
Polka, you try too! Okay! Wait... oh...

1687
01:21:25,970 --> 01:21:27,770
Okay, this, this, this, this...

1688
01:21:28,570 --> 01:21:30,570
Hot, hot, hot! It's hot!

1689
01:21:30,570 --> 01:21:32,340
Can't break it yet. Still hot?

1690
01:21:32,340 --> 01:21:33,970
It's hot, it's hot, it's hot!

1691
01:21:33,970 --> 01:21:35,970
Hot, hot, hot! Hot, hot, hot!

1692
01:21:35,970 --> 01:21:37,970
Hot, hot, hot! Hot, hot, hot!

1693
01:21:37,970 --> 01:21:39,970
It's hot — Polka's on fire!

1694
01:21:39,970 --> 01:21:41,770


1695
01:21:41,770 --> 01:21:43,770
Polka was literally on fire there.

1696
01:21:43,770 --> 01:21:49,570
She's combusting.

1697
01:21:49,570 --> 01:21:51,370
Still...

1698
01:21:51,370 --> 01:21:53,170
I hear an animal, Luna!

1699
01:21:54,970 --> 01:21:56,970
There it is! A boar!

1700
01:21:56,970 --> 01:21:58,770
Piggy piggy! Got it, got it, got it!

1701
01:21:58,770 --> 01:22:04,440
This thing is heavy.

1702
01:22:04,440 --> 01:22:05,440
The ammo count is insane.

1703
01:22:05,440 --> 01:22:09,140
The heli — should we go for the heli too?

1704
01:22:09,140 --> 01:22:11,040
Polka, try defending with this!

1705
01:22:11,040 --> 01:22:13,840
It holds 100 rounds?! That's crazy!

1706
01:22:13,840 --> 01:22:16,640
Hey, can we shoot that helicopter?

1707
01:22:16,640 --> 01:22:20,240
Since when are you so bold?

1708
01:22:20,240 --> 01:22:22,040
Well, I mean...

1709
01:22:22,040 --> 01:22:24,540
It's a bit far away though, isn't it?

1710
01:22:24,540 --> 01:22:29,360
I feel so powerful right now.

1711
01:22:29,360 --> 01:22:31,700
It's like a real machine gun!

1712
01:22:31,700 --> 01:22:35,340
But it drifts way up.

1713
01:22:35,340 --> 01:22:37,860
The recoil is intense.

1714
01:22:37,860 --> 01:22:40,440
I wonder if there's something to reduce the recoil.

1715
01:22:40,440 --> 01:22:43,980
Maybe you can mod it somehow?

1716
01:22:43,980 --> 01:22:46,500
Incredible.

1717
01:22:46,500 --> 01:22:48,940
The M249.

1718
01:22:48,940 --> 01:22:52,960
The M249 is no joke!

1719
01:22:52,960 --> 01:22:55,640
Whoa, it was shooting at us from all the way over there?!

1720
01:22:55,640 --> 01:22:57,340
That's awful.

1721
01:22:57,340 --> 01:22:58,940
Unforgivable.

1722
01:22:58,940 --> 01:23:00,120
Incredible.

1723
01:23:00,120 --> 01:23:04,860
I can't forgive that tank.

1724
01:23:04,860 --> 01:23:06,960
What if you crouch while shooting?

1725
01:23:06,960 --> 01:23:08,640
Does crouching make it easier to aim?

1726
01:23:08,640 --> 01:23:11,500
Yeah, it might reduce the recoil a bit.

1727
01:23:11,500 --> 01:23:15,580
I honestly didn't think it would drop.

1728
01:23:15,580 --> 01:23:18,760
Polka totally believed it would though!

1729
01:23:18,760 --> 01:23:21,970
I knew it! I just knew it!

1730
01:23:21,970 --> 01:23:26,970
Take that, tank!

1731
01:23:32,800 --> 01:23:40,800
Whoa, it's in pieces!

1732
01:23:40,800 --> 01:23:42,900
Yay!

1733
01:23:42,900 --> 01:23:45,900
We did it!

1734
01:23:45,900 --> 01:23:47,600
Everything just fell right out.

1735
01:23:47,600 --> 01:23:51,300
Got the metal fragments too. Nice!

1736
01:23:51,300 --> 01:23:53,260
Wow...

1737
01:23:53,260 --> 01:23:55,500
Victory as-is!

1738
01:23:55,500 --> 01:23:57,960
That was amazing!

1739
01:23:57,960 --> 01:23:59,860
We won!

1740
01:23:59,860 --> 01:24:01,360
We did it!

1741
01:24:01,360 --> 01:24:04,140
We actually won!

1742
01:24:04,140 --> 01:24:04,660
Wah! Wah! Woohoo!

1743
01:24:04,660 --> 01:24:06,420
We won!

1744
01:24:06,420 --> 01:24:10,830
Wooohooo!

1745
01:24:10,830 --> 01:24:12,550
holoRUST victory!

1746
01:24:12,550 --> 01:24:15,130
Victory!

1747
01:24:15,130 --> 01:24:16,790
Amazing!

1748
01:24:16,790 --> 01:24:19,270
That's the M249 for you!

1749
01:24:19,270 --> 01:24:23,350
Right?! And it came on the very last day!

1750
01:24:23,350 --> 01:24:26,390
We were a bit of a slow start, huh.

1751
01:24:26,390 --> 01:24:27,950
We really were.

1752
01:24:27,950 --> 01:24:31,110
We were slow starters, but...

1753
01:24:31,110 --> 01:24:33,890
We won't even get to show off this thing properly.

1754
01:24:33,890 --> 01:24:39,210
Hopefully in the night session...

1755
01:24:39,210 --> 01:24:40,330
Somehow...

1756
01:24:40,330 --> 01:24:43,490
Are we doing something with this in the night session?

1757
01:24:43,490 --> 01:24:45,230
I mean, there's nothing really planned...

1758
01:24:45,230 --> 01:24:49,650
But hey, we took down the tank!

1759
01:24:49,650 --> 01:24:50,870
That's incredible.

1760
01:24:50,870 --> 01:24:52,870
We really made the most of it!

1761
01:24:53,350 --> 01:24:55,650
We did it!

1762
01:24:55,650 --> 01:24:58,970
This time we managed to do a lot of things we couldn't do last time.

1763
01:24:58,970 --> 01:25:01,170
Polka really pulled through!

1764
01:25:01,170 --> 01:25:05,130
It was my first time fighting the tank!

1765
01:25:05,130 --> 01:25:05,410
Yeah!

1766
01:25:05,410 --> 01:25:09,230
Doing this repeatedly would take years off your life.

1767
01:25:09,230 --> 01:25:10,470
For real.

1768
01:25:10,470 --> 01:25:12,530
My lifespan is just draining away.

1769
01:25:12,530 --> 01:25:14,210
That's just how it is.

1770
01:25:14,210 --> 01:25:16,250
It looks easy but it's actually brutal.

1771
01:25:16,250 --> 01:25:20,120
I mean, to be fair—

1772
01:25:20,120 --> 01:25:22,180
the tank was basically stuck the whole time,

1773
01:25:22,180 --> 01:25:24,720
so it felt a little easier than usual.

1774
01:25:24,720 --> 01:25:26,000
That's true too.

1775
01:25:26,000 --> 01:25:27,780
It wasn't moving, after all.

1776
01:25:27,780 --> 01:25:29,640
Oh, hello there, helicopter!

1777
01:25:29,640 --> 01:25:31,340
Is the heli coming again?

1778
01:25:31,340 --> 01:25:33,380
It's a small one—

1779
01:25:33,380 --> 01:25:35,240
Nah, it's not coming.

1780
01:25:35,240 --> 01:25:38,750
It's not coming, it's not coming.

1781
01:25:38,750 --> 01:25:41,710
Since it's just us out here, the heli keeps targeting us.

1782
01:25:41,710 --> 01:25:44,810
All eyes on us.

1783
01:25:44,810 --> 01:25:46,950
Have we done anything wrong?

1784
01:25:46,950 --> 01:25:48,510
We have.

1785
01:25:48,510 --> 01:25:50,310
We have.

1786
01:25:50,310 --> 01:25:52,310
We did the tank.

1787
01:25:52,310 --> 01:25:54,220
We took down the tank.

1788
01:25:54,220 --> 01:25:56,110
But hey, Kanata—

1789
01:25:56,110 --> 01:25:58,110
Kanata, you still can't log in today either, right?

1790
01:25:58,110 --> 01:26:00,110
I at least want to report the news to her.

1791
01:26:00,110 --> 01:26:01,910
Yeah, for sure.

1792
01:26:01,910 --> 01:26:03,910
It was her dream, after all.

1793
01:26:03,910 --> 01:26:07,710
To think that we'd get an M249—

1794
01:26:07,710 --> 01:26:11,710
She said she wanted an M249 from the golden egg.

1795
01:26:11,710 --> 01:26:13,510
She said that.

1796
01:26:13,510 --> 01:26:16,510
And we got one from the tank instead!

1797
01:26:17,640 --> 01:26:18,640
Close enough!

1798
01:26:18,640 --> 01:26:24,990
Who's that over there?

1799
01:26:24,990 --> 01:26:26,790
Shall we head back?

1800
01:26:26,790 --> 01:26:28,590
They said it looks similar!

1801
01:26:28,590 --> 01:26:30,590
They said it looks similar — that's actually a compliment!

1802
01:26:30,590 --> 01:26:31,590
Looks similar, huh.

1803
01:26:31,590 --> 01:26:35,390
Haven't used the recycler yet.

1804
01:26:35,390 --> 01:26:39,990
It's back again!

1805
01:26:39,990 --> 01:26:44,210
The Egg Hunt!

1806
01:26:44,210 --> 01:26:45,210
It's Egg Hunt time!

1807
01:26:45,210 --> 01:26:47,210
Fun fun Egg Hunt!

1808
01:26:48,010 --> 01:26:50,010
We don't have time for this right now!

1809
01:26:50,010 --> 01:26:53,010
Seriously!

1810
01:26:53,010 --> 01:26:54,510
Right now we're just having a great time—

1811
01:26:54,510 --> 01:26:58,810
We just finished the tank fight and we're finally breathing again.

1812
01:26:58,810 --> 01:27:02,410
I'm so glad we pulled it off.

1813
01:27:02,410 --> 01:27:04,410
Right, seriously.

1814
01:27:04,410 --> 01:27:05,410
Yesterday was rough.

1815
01:27:05,410 --> 01:27:09,710
The zombie attack was intense.

1816
01:27:09,710 --> 01:27:11,910
It really was a zombie attack situation.

1817
01:27:15,140 --> 01:27:17,050
Are you okay? Think you can make it to the shooting range?

1818
01:27:17,050 --> 01:27:19,050
Heading to the shooting range now.

1819
01:27:19,050 --> 01:27:20,050
Nice, nice!

1820
01:27:20,050 --> 01:27:23,380
Yay!

1821
01:27:23,380 --> 01:27:24,380
Yay!

1822
01:27:24,380 --> 01:27:28,680
Passing the torch of life.

1823
01:27:28,680 --> 01:27:29,480
The torch of life.

1824
01:27:29,480 --> 01:27:30,480
Koupo's here.

1825
01:27:30,480 --> 01:27:31,480
Right, right.

1826
01:27:31,480 --> 01:27:33,280
Koupo's there—

1827
01:27:33,280 --> 01:27:34,280
Yep, yep.

1828
01:27:34,280 --> 01:27:35,080


1829
01:27:35,080 --> 01:27:36,880
That was a nice move though.

1830
01:27:36,880 --> 01:27:42,100
Well, for both sides, the bug—

1831
01:27:42,100 --> 01:27:44,100
It's basically a win-by-bug situation.

1832
01:27:44,100 --> 01:27:47,460
Same for us — we won because the tank got stuck.

1833
01:27:47,460 --> 01:27:48,360
That's true.

1834
01:27:48,360 --> 01:27:50,200
50-50.

1835
01:27:50,200 --> 01:27:52,920
Fair's fair.

1836
01:27:52,920 --> 01:27:56,540
That kind of thing just happens with a crash like that.

1837
01:27:56,540 --> 01:27:57,920
OK.

1838
01:27:57,920 --> 01:28:03,160
We managed to beat Finny though!

1839
01:28:03,160 --> 01:28:04,460
I'm fully satisfied.

1840
01:28:04,460 --> 01:28:07,460
Are we fighting?

1841
01:28:07,460 --> 01:28:11,890
I'm fully done with this!

1842
01:28:11,890 --> 01:28:13,210
Last stretch!

1843
01:28:14,640 --> 01:28:18,810
There's a heli!

1844
01:28:18,810 --> 01:28:20,070
The heli's here!

1845
01:28:20,070 --> 01:28:21,050
Train Yard!

1846
01:28:21,050 --> 01:28:22,690
Straight ahead, straight ahead!

1847
01:28:22,690 --> 01:28:24,090
Straight!

1848
01:28:24,090 --> 01:28:25,610
Not the heli — the tank, the tank!

1849
01:28:25,610 --> 01:28:28,010
Turn right, right!

1850
01:28:28,010 --> 01:28:31,370
I can see home already!

1851
01:28:31,370 --> 01:28:32,010
We're so close!

1852
01:28:32,010 --> 01:28:32,790
Right!

1853
01:28:32,790 --> 01:28:34,750
What's the heli doing?

1854
01:28:34,750 --> 01:28:36,510
What's the heli doing?

1855
01:28:36,510 --> 01:28:38,930
Heli, stop it!

1856
01:28:38,930 --> 01:28:40,350
Heli, stop it!

1857
01:28:40,350 --> 01:28:41,350
Stop it, heli!

1858
01:28:41,350 --> 01:28:44,150
Left, left — straight then left!

1859
01:28:44,150 --> 01:28:46,950
Wait, the heli — the heli's here!

1860
01:28:46,950 --> 01:28:47,950
The heli went toward you!

1861
01:28:47,950 --> 01:28:50,750
It turned back this way!

1862
01:28:50,750 --> 01:28:51,750
Straight then left!

1863
01:28:51,750 --> 01:28:52,550
The heli...

1864
01:28:52,550 --> 01:28:57,920
This is bad!

1865
01:28:57,920 --> 01:29:00,720
What?! It blew up again!

1866
01:29:00,720 --> 01:29:01,720
Again!

1867
01:29:01,720 --> 01:29:03,520
What?!

1868
01:29:03,520 --> 01:29:08,870
The heli is still here!

1869
01:29:14,500 --> 01:29:17,320
What are we supposed to do?!

1870
01:29:17,320 --> 01:29:18,320
Seriously!

1871
01:29:18,120 --> 01:29:20,120
For real!

1872
01:29:20,120 --> 01:29:28,360
Dying to an explosion is the worst!

1873
01:29:28,360 --> 01:29:32,720
I don't want to die to an explosion!

1874
01:29:32,720 --> 01:29:34,720
I'm going home!

1875
01:29:34,720 --> 01:29:37,320
That thing is the absolute worst!

1876
01:29:37,320 --> 01:29:41,720
Unforgivable!

1877
01:29:44,030 --> 01:29:45,640
I thought I was starting to like the heli a little, but...

1878
01:29:45,430 --> 01:29:48,230
Hey, the car—

1879
01:29:48,230 --> 01:29:51,030
Hey, get in the back, Luna!

1880
01:29:51,030 --> 01:29:51,830
Is the heli gone?

1881
01:29:51,830 --> 01:29:52,830
Not sure.

1882
01:29:52,830 --> 01:29:53,630
Is it gone?

1883
01:29:53,630 --> 01:29:55,430
Get in the back.

1884
01:29:55,430 --> 01:29:56,430
Got in, got in!

1885
01:29:56,430 --> 01:29:58,430
We'll show it we're harmless!

1886
01:29:58,430 --> 01:30:02,830
Ugh!

1887
01:30:02,830 --> 01:30:09,960
The camping car got destroyed again!

1888
01:30:09,960 --> 01:30:11,760
Did everything blow up?

1889
01:30:11,760 --> 01:30:14,560
It just keeps getting destroyed!

1890
01:30:14,560 --> 01:30:17,360
Whoa! It's a sea of fire!

1891
01:30:17,360 --> 01:30:19,160
Which one is it?

1892
01:30:19,160 --> 01:30:20,960
Something's coming.

1893
01:30:20,960 --> 01:30:21,760
Someone's here.

1894
01:30:21,760 --> 01:30:23,560
Huh? What is?

1895
01:30:23,560 --> 01:30:24,360
Huh?

1896
01:30:24,360 --> 01:30:26,160
There's someone here.

1897
01:30:26,160 --> 01:30:27,960
Hello!

1898
01:30:27,960 --> 01:30:28,960
Are you okay?

1899
01:30:28,960 --> 01:30:32,760
Our bodies are there!

1900
01:30:32,760 --> 01:30:35,760
Oh no! Thank you! Did you take out the bear?

1901
01:30:35,760 --> 01:30:37,490
Over there, over there!

1902
01:30:37,490 --> 01:30:39,360
Oh, the bear just died on its own.

1903
01:30:39,360 --> 01:30:41,160
The bear just died on its own — okay.

1904
01:30:41,160 --> 01:30:42,960
Because, probably...

1905
01:30:42,960 --> 01:30:46,960
It came to eat this person and got burned in the fire.

1906
01:30:46,960 --> 01:30:48,760
Polka's stuff...

1907
01:30:48,760 --> 01:30:53,540
Thanks, we're fine — but the camping car got destroyed.

1908
01:30:53,540 --> 01:30:55,160
Um...

1909
01:30:55,160 --> 01:30:57,960
Oh no, that's rough. Sorry about that.

1910
01:30:57,960 --> 01:31:03,820
I was just logging in and lying there when I heard this huge noise...

1911
01:31:04,120 --> 01:31:06,510
Oh wait, this is Polka's stuff.

1912
01:31:06,510 --> 01:31:08,510
Sorry for scaring you!

1913
01:31:08,510 --> 01:31:10,310
It's okay!

1914
01:31:10,310 --> 01:31:12,310
Totally fine!

1915
01:31:12,310 --> 01:31:14,310
Good, good — totally fine!

1916
01:31:14,310 --> 01:31:16,110
Where's Kanata's body?

1917
01:31:16,110 --> 01:31:17,910
Oh, is this it?

1918
01:31:17,910 --> 01:31:19,910
There are three bodies here, so we should be fine.

1919
01:31:19,910 --> 01:31:21,710
Just in case.

1920
01:31:21,710 --> 01:31:24,530
The bodies look okay.

1921
01:31:24,530 --> 01:31:27,450
Ugh...

1922
01:31:27,450 --> 01:31:29,450
Oh man, that scared me!

1923
01:31:29,450 --> 01:31:31,250
What the heck?!

1924
01:31:31,250 --> 01:31:33,200
What was that thing?!

1925
01:31:33,200 --> 01:31:34,050
Anti!

1926
01:31:34,050 --> 01:31:35,850
Hime!

1927
01:31:35,850 --> 01:31:39,450
We died way too many times!

1928
01:31:48,660 --> 01:31:51,660
And it wasn't even the tank that got us!

1929
01:31:51,660 --> 01:31:55,540
Was that a mama bear and her cub?

1930
01:31:55,540 --> 01:31:58,340
Seriously, what the heck?!

1931
01:31:58,340 --> 01:32:03,940
This time we took damage from something that wasn't even the tank.

1932
01:32:03,940 --> 01:32:04,940
I'm okay though!

1933
01:32:04,940 --> 01:32:05,940
I'm fine!

1934
01:32:06,940 --> 01:32:12,850
A second bear showed up, but I'm okay!

1935
01:32:12,850 --> 01:32:15,030
Hold on—

1936
01:32:15,030 --> 01:32:18,450
Sorry for causing a ruckus right in the neighborhood!

1937
01:32:18,450 --> 01:32:21,810
Thank you!

1938
01:32:21,810 --> 01:32:23,910
The patrol heli is coming!

1939
01:32:23,910 --> 01:32:27,550
Give me back my M249!

1940
01:32:27,550 --> 01:32:31,590
Wait, wait!

1941
01:32:31,590 --> 01:32:34,470
It's targeting me, what do I do?!

1942
01:32:34,470 --> 01:32:35,130
Run!

1943
01:32:35,130 --> 01:32:37,710
We've left way too many bodies in front of Niko-tan's place.

1944
01:32:37,710 --> 01:32:38,730
I know, right?

1945
01:32:38,730 --> 01:32:42,430
What if we hit Niko-tan's house?!

1946
01:32:42,430 --> 01:32:45,670
This is such an accident waiting to happen.

1947
01:32:45,670 --> 01:32:48,570
A bear?! Wait, are you kidding me?!

1948
01:32:48,570 --> 01:32:52,690
I didn't expect two bears to show up!

1949
01:32:52,690 --> 01:32:54,570
Is this Kanatan's body?

1950
01:32:54,570 --> 01:32:55,290
This one?

1951
01:32:55,290 --> 01:32:56,670
Wait, which one is Kanatan?

1952
01:32:56,670 --> 01:32:57,390
That one, that one!

1953
01:32:57,390 --> 01:32:58,330
The blue one!

1954
01:32:58,330 --> 01:33:00,330
Oh, this one, this one!

1955
01:33:00,330 --> 01:33:03,130
Are you kidding me?!

1956
01:33:04,150 --> 01:33:05,150
Seriously, that heli...

1957
01:33:05,150 --> 01:33:06,150
I'm literally tearing up.

1958
01:33:06,150 --> 01:33:08,950
That thing is totally a stalker, I swear.

1959
01:33:08,950 --> 01:33:09,950
What is its deal?!

1960
01:33:09,950 --> 01:33:13,550
It's way too obsessed with us.

1961
01:33:13,550 --> 01:33:15,350
This is Poh-Poh's body, right?

1962
01:33:15,350 --> 01:33:16,350
Yeah, which one?

1963
01:33:16,350 --> 01:33:18,150
Under Poh-Poh.

1964
01:33:18,150 --> 01:33:19,150
Uh, this one?

1965
01:33:19,150 --> 01:33:20,150
Oh, but there's nothing on it.

1966
01:33:20,150 --> 01:33:21,950
This one says Himemori on it.

1967
01:33:21,950 --> 01:33:22,950
This one's Poh-Poh.

1968
01:33:22,950 --> 01:33:23,950
Oh, this is Poh-Poh!

1969
01:33:23,950 --> 01:33:25,950
There are bodies rolling all over the place down here.

1970
01:33:25,950 --> 01:33:27,750
This is the worst.

1971
01:33:27,750 --> 01:33:30,550
And the camping car got wrecked too.

1972
01:33:30,550 --> 01:33:31,550
Actually, it's not destroyed.

1973
01:33:31,550 --> 01:33:34,530
Looks like it can be repaired! Better than last time, at least.

1974
01:33:34,530 --> 01:33:36,150
Oh, you're right!

1975
01:33:36,150 --> 01:33:39,550
Oh, scary...

1976
01:33:39,550 --> 01:33:41,550
But still, you know...

1977
01:33:41,550 --> 01:33:46,530
Can we fix it?

1978
01:33:46,530 --> 01:33:47,370
*hammering sounds*

1979
01:33:47,370 --> 01:33:49,370
Hmm...

1980
01:33:49,370 --> 01:33:54,650
That's scary — I'm hearing sounds again.

1981
01:33:54,650 --> 01:33:56,650
Those sounds are scary, wait wait wait!

1982
01:33:56,650 --> 01:33:57,910
Is the heli coming?

1983
01:33:57,910 --> 01:33:59,530
I don't know, it's close to me.

1984
01:33:59,530 --> 01:34:02,150
It's just nearby, just nearby, just nearby—

1985
01:34:02,150 --> 01:34:04,250
Just nearby, just nearby — I'm scared too!

1986
01:34:04,250 --> 01:34:11,790
I can't tell anymore... we've been attacked so many times I've lost track.

1987
01:34:11,790 --> 01:34:15,430
What do those things even want?

1988
01:34:15,430 --> 01:34:17,390
To kill us. That's it.

1989
01:34:17,390 --> 01:34:19,030
I'm scared!

1990
01:34:19,030 --> 01:34:22,070
We can't repair it — we're out of wood.

1991
01:34:22,070 --> 01:34:24,730
Yeah, we used up all our wood, we really did.

1992
01:34:24,730 --> 01:34:29,390
We hit it and got some metal on it though.

1993
01:34:29,390 --> 01:34:35,530
We're close enough to just walk back, it's fine.

1994
01:34:35,530 --> 01:34:37,290
True enough.

1995
01:34:37,290 --> 01:34:40,970
Maybe we don't even need the car anymore.

1996
01:34:40,970 --> 01:34:43,850
We worked so hard to get it too.

1997
01:34:43,850 --> 01:34:51,390
We lost two cars in just a few hours today.

1998
01:34:51,390 --> 01:34:53,380
We went through them way too fast.

1999
01:34:53,380 --> 01:34:56,270
They got wrecked so quickly!

2000
01:34:56,270 --> 01:34:59,470
Gone in a flash.

2001
01:34:59,470 --> 01:35:01,470
That broke way too fast!

2002
01:35:01,470 --> 01:35:04,470
Well, we're abandoning this one. Thanks for the ride.

2003
01:35:04,470 --> 01:35:06,470
Just leaving it here.

2004
01:35:06,470 --> 01:35:13,030
It's already half-buried anyway.

2005
01:35:13,030 --> 01:35:18,310
Let's just head home.

2006
01:35:20,310 --> 01:35:23,110
There's junk scattered everywhere!

2007
01:35:23,110 --> 01:35:25,610
Right in front of our junior's house!

2008
01:35:25,610 --> 01:35:27,610
Getting shot up like that!

2009
01:35:27,610 --> 01:35:29,610
And leaving trash behind too!

2010
01:35:29,610 --> 01:35:31,410
Ugh, come on...

2011
01:35:31,410 --> 01:35:34,710
We were so close to making it!

2012
01:35:34,710 --> 01:35:35,710
I know, right?!

2013
01:35:35,710 --> 01:35:38,210
We were right around the corner!

2014
01:35:38,210 --> 01:35:40,210
My place was getting bombed too, so...

2015
01:35:40,210 --> 01:35:41,710
Thank goodness!

2016
01:35:41,710 --> 01:35:43,210
Niko-tan, thank goodness!

2017
01:35:43,210 --> 01:35:44,210
You're safe!

2018
01:35:44,210 --> 01:35:45,010
We need to bring Niko-tan

2019
01:35:45,010 --> 01:35:46,990
some kind of apology gift.

2020
01:35:46,990 --> 01:35:48,810
She nearly got caught in the crossfire.

2021
01:35:48,810 --> 01:35:53,810
Niko-tan's house was seriously getting bombed — that was bad.

2022
01:35:53,810 --> 01:35:55,610
It really was.

2023
01:35:55,610 --> 01:35:59,410
We have to bring her something to apologize.

2024
01:35:59,410 --> 01:36:01,210
What would be good, I wonder?

2025
01:36:01,210 --> 01:36:03,210
Good work, everyone.

2026
01:36:03,210 --> 01:36:08,010
Kanata, bring out the M249!

2027
01:36:08,010 --> 01:36:10,810
You have an M249?

2028
01:36:10,810 --> 01:36:13,410
Kanata's so happy!

2029
01:36:13,410 --> 01:36:16,400
Yay, M249!

2030
01:36:16,400 --> 01:36:18,330
Don't point that at me — it's so heavy-looking!

2031
01:36:18,330 --> 01:36:22,590
The one you've always wanted,

2032
01:36:22,590 --> 01:36:25,030
we went and got it for you!

2033
01:36:25,030 --> 01:36:27,950
At the cost of many, many lives.

2034
01:36:27,950 --> 01:36:31,670
We died so many times today too.

2035
01:36:31,670 --> 01:36:32,750
It's kind of ridiculous.

2036
01:36:32,750 --> 01:36:35,910
We said it was going to go smoothly, didn't we?

2037
01:36:35,910 --> 01:36:36,550
After all that buildup...

2038
01:36:36,550 --> 01:36:38,710
We died so pointlessly.

2039
01:36:38,710 --> 01:36:39,610
We really did.

2040
01:36:39,610 --> 01:36:41,990
We died this many times to stuff that wasn't even the tank!

2041
01:36:41,990 --> 01:36:46,290
We died more to non-tank stuff than the actual tank.

2042
01:36:46,290 --> 01:36:50,590
What is going on?

2043
01:36:50,590 --> 01:36:54,170
We did it though!

2044
01:36:54,170 --> 01:36:55,970
Well, "we did it" isn't quite right...

2045
01:36:55,970 --> 01:36:56,730
We did do it.

2046
01:36:56,730 --> 01:36:59,110
But it was those guys who actually did it.

2047
01:36:59,110 --> 01:37:00,330
The worst.

2048
01:37:00,330 --> 01:37:03,040
Unbelievable.

2049
01:37:03,040 --> 01:37:08,140
Not funny at all.

2050
01:37:08,140 --> 01:37:17,890
Hehehe... that was so fun though. Crazy things happen in life, huh?

2051
01:37:17,890 --> 01:37:27,890
I'm glad to be alive... well, we died but it worked out, so... it's hard to put into words.

2052
01:37:31,020 --> 01:37:37,630
Living life gives you all kinds of experiences... even if we did die.

2053
01:37:37,630 --> 01:37:41,430
This and this.

2054
01:37:41,430 --> 01:37:45,230
We did grow a little bit though.

2055
01:37:45,230 --> 01:37:47,030
We did!

2056
01:37:47,030 --> 01:37:50,830
We ended up with way more rocket launcher ammo than before.

2057
01:37:50,830 --> 01:37:53,630
More than when we came?

2058
01:37:53,630 --> 01:37:55,430
Maybe not quite that many.

2059
01:37:55,430 --> 01:37:56,430
Did we pick some up?

2060
01:37:56,430 --> 01:37:59,430
Yeah, we picked some up — 6 rockets.

2061
01:37:59,430 --> 01:38:01,230
That's quite a few then.

2062
01:38:01,230 --> 01:38:03,230
And homing missiles too.

2063
01:38:03,230 --> 01:38:07,090
Oh! So then... but wait, what was it...

2064
01:38:07,090 --> 01:38:17,090
What was it called — some kind of rocket — is that for the tank, or the military base? Oh, the missile launcher thing. That's PvP stuff too, isn't it?

2065
01:38:18,160 --> 01:38:22,590
We don't need the launcher itself. The ones we're not using...

2066
01:38:22,590 --> 01:38:26,370
I'm not trading unused ones away.

2067
01:38:26,870 --> 01:38:36,090
Doesn't that have a cooldown too? The military base one...

2068
01:38:36,090 --> 01:38:44,310
Oh really? There were people at the military base too, right? You hack the missile computer there and...

2069
01:38:44,310 --> 01:38:52,560
Whaaaat? I had no idea! I can't do that. Maybe in PvP someone could pull it off, but...

2070
01:38:52,560 --> 01:38:59,910
Using 12 of these... is this the MLRS rocket? Yeah, something like that.

2071
01:38:59,910 --> 01:39:05,970
I'd never use that many. It's the one you fire from the American base, right? Yeah, yeah, exactly.

2072
01:39:05,970 --> 01:39:12,810
We don't need that many. We're not doing that, are we? That's way too much.

2073
01:39:13,350 --> 01:39:17,350
If this were PvP, we'd be absolutely dominating right now.

2074
01:39:17,350 --> 01:39:21,330
Guns in hand and everything.

2075
01:39:21,330 --> 01:39:24,320
True, but I still don't really know how any of that works.

2076
01:39:24,320 --> 01:39:26,320
My skills just haven't caught up yet.

2077
01:39:26,320 --> 01:39:32,280
The helicopter's back.

2078
01:39:32,280 --> 01:39:33,280
Ugh, not the helicopter again...

2079
01:39:33,280 --> 01:39:37,680
It's clearly figured out where we are.

2080
01:39:37,680 --> 01:39:39,480
Should we try shooting at it?

2081
01:39:43,250 --> 01:39:44,880
Wait, Luna?

2082
01:39:44,880 --> 01:39:46,880
Homing missile! Homing missile! Homing missile!

2083
01:39:46,880 --> 01:39:49,680
No matter how many times they've taken us out—

2084
01:39:49,680 --> 01:39:51,680
Homing missile! Where did we put the homing missiles?

2085
01:39:51,680 --> 01:39:58,140
The homing missiles should be over there, they should be there.

2086
01:39:58,140 --> 01:40:00,080
Isn't it getting closer? Like—

2087
01:40:00,080 --> 01:40:03,880
It's targeting us!

2088
01:40:03,880 --> 01:40:06,680
The homing thing— where is it?

2089
01:40:06,680 --> 01:40:08,460
Homing missile!

2090
01:40:08,460 --> 01:40:13,260
What's this? Ammo? What do I load it into?

2091
01:40:13,260 --> 01:40:17,820
Is this a rocket launcher... a rocket launcher? A homing launcher...

2092
01:40:17,820 --> 01:40:22,800
What do I attach it to... wait, what can you fire a rocket launcher from?

2093
01:40:22,800 --> 01:40:25,940
A dedicated launcher? Oh, I think we had one.

2094
01:40:25,940 --> 01:40:29,040
Like a homing launcher?

2095
01:40:29,040 --> 01:40:29,860
Do we have one?

2096
01:40:29,860 --> 01:40:32,320
We do!

2097
01:40:32,320 --> 01:40:34,350
This house has everything.

2098
01:40:34,350 --> 01:40:35,820
It's kind of scary.

2099
01:40:35,820 --> 01:40:37,020
This, this, this, this!

2100
01:40:37,020 --> 01:40:39,920
If we fire near the house it'll get destroyed, so

2101
01:40:39,920 --> 01:40:42,420
move a bit away and load it up.

2102
01:40:42,420 --> 01:40:44,520
We only have one, by the way.

2103
01:40:44,520 --> 01:40:47,020
Wait, let me see if I can craft another one.

2104
01:40:47,020 --> 01:40:49,020
Hurry or the helicopter will—

2105
01:40:49,020 --> 01:40:50,420
The helicopter's going to leave!

2106
01:40:50,420 --> 01:40:51,820
Well, the helicopter leaving is actually a good thing.

2107
01:40:51,820 --> 01:40:55,420
It's only targeting us, so—

2108
01:40:55,420 --> 01:41:00,100
Let's try not to bother Niko, let's move away a bit.

2109
01:41:00,100 --> 01:41:09,160
Can I craft a homing launcher right now? Is it craftable?

2110
01:41:09,160 --> 01:41:17,540
If I research it— we've been throwing money at everything, so yeah, I can research it!

2111
01:41:20,400 --> 01:41:24,840
Alright, let's make one. Time to show that helicopter some payback.

2112
01:41:24,840 --> 01:41:26,080
For real.

2113
01:41:26,080 --> 01:41:29,260
We'll track it down with a homing missile.

2114
01:41:29,260 --> 01:41:32,300
Let's bring two homing missiles.

2115
01:41:32,300 --> 01:41:34,600
Sounds good.

2116
01:41:34,600 --> 01:41:36,720
Let's do it!

2117
01:41:36,720 --> 01:41:42,480
Time to avenge everything we've been through!

2118
01:41:42,480 --> 01:41:47,300
Wait, we need a CCTV camera for this.

2119
01:41:47,300 --> 01:41:48,700
We have a CCTV camera!

2120
01:41:48,700 --> 01:41:50,400
Just one?

2121
01:41:50,400 --> 01:41:55,020
CCTV camera.

2122
01:41:55,020 --> 01:41:56,920
Just one.

2123
01:41:56,920 --> 01:41:58,220
I dropped it, I dropped it here.

2124
01:41:58,220 --> 01:41:59,920
Oh wait, we also need pipes.

2125
01:41:59,920 --> 01:42:01,220
Do we have pipes? Still?

2126
01:42:01,220 --> 01:42:02,920
I used all the pipes.

2127
01:42:02,920 --> 01:42:07,020
It's over!

2128
01:42:07,020 --> 01:42:08,320
We can't use the missiles.

2129
01:42:08,320 --> 01:42:09,820
There are 13 in the trash can!

2130
01:42:09,820 --> 01:42:12,520
Pick up that CCTV over there.

2131
01:42:12,520 --> 01:42:13,420
Got it.

2132
01:42:13,420 --> 01:42:14,920
There are 13 in the trash can.

2133
01:42:15,520 --> 01:42:16,520
Wh-what?!

2134
01:42:16,520 --> 01:42:17,220
Huh?

2135
01:42:17,220 --> 01:42:17,920
Where are the CCTV pipes?

2136
01:42:17,920 --> 01:42:18,720
Here, right here.

2137
01:42:18,720 --> 01:42:19,720
This, this, this, this!

2138
01:42:19,720 --> 01:42:20,220
At your feet.

2139
01:42:20,220 --> 01:42:20,920
At your feet.

2140
01:42:20,920 --> 01:42:23,120
They're at your feet.

2141
01:42:23,120 --> 01:42:24,620
There are 13 pipes in the trash can.

2142
01:42:24,620 --> 01:42:25,720
13 pipes.

2143
01:42:25,720 --> 01:42:27,720
13 pipes, bam bam bam.

2144
01:42:27,720 --> 01:42:29,120
There are 13 pipes, bam bam bam.

2145
01:42:29,120 --> 01:42:31,320
Where's the helicopter now?

2146
01:42:31,320 --> 01:42:33,720
With this—

2147
01:42:33,720 --> 01:42:36,220
Has the helicopter moved away a bit?

2148
01:42:36,220 --> 01:42:36,820
Let's lure the helicopter over!

2149
01:42:36,820 --> 01:42:38,020
Hey, helicopter!

2150
01:42:38,020 --> 01:42:39,920
Heliiii!

2151
01:42:39,920 --> 01:42:41,520
Heliiii?

2152
01:42:41,520 --> 01:42:42,820
It'll come, right?

2153
01:42:43,520 --> 01:42:45,320
Ugh, it's an NPC~

2154
01:42:45,320 --> 01:42:49,220
Well, if we do it here the house will get destroyed.

2155
01:42:49,220 --> 01:42:53,680
We don't want the helicopter destroying the house.

2156
01:42:53,680 --> 01:42:55,330
Yeah, fair enough.

2157
01:42:55,330 --> 01:42:58,020
I'll go pick a fight with the NPC.

2158
01:42:58,020 --> 01:42:59,920
With this—

2159
01:42:59,920 --> 01:43:03,380
Oh wait, the CCTV—

2160
01:43:03,380 --> 01:43:05,380
We can only craft one CCTV.

2161
01:43:05,380 --> 01:43:10,220
Yeah, Kanata—

2162
01:43:11,590 --> 01:43:12,590
Did we get it?

2163
01:43:12,590 --> 01:43:19,060
What? The helicopter sound stopped — that's the worst

2164
01:43:19,060 --> 01:43:21,340


2165
01:43:21,340 --> 01:43:24,030


2166
01:43:24,030 --> 01:43:25,290


2167
01:43:25,290 --> 01:43:26,650
With me?

2168
01:43:26,650 --> 01:43:28,770
I thought we actually got it!

2169
01:43:28,770 --> 01:43:33,460
What happened?

2170
01:43:33,460 --> 01:43:35,560
Huh? I was messing around with the NPCs

2171
01:43:35,560 --> 01:43:37,140
Ah, I see

2172
01:43:37,140 --> 01:43:39,940
She's hopeless, Polka is

2173
01:43:39,940 --> 01:43:40,940


2174
01:43:42,320 --> 01:43:44,220
Did you get hit? Are you okay?

2175
01:43:44,220 --> 01:43:46,240
Yeah, I totally got hit

2176
01:43:46,240 --> 01:43:48,620
Yeah, Polka just keeps getting wrecked

2177
01:43:48,620 --> 01:43:50,120
Because I'm weak

2178
01:43:50,120 --> 01:43:53,920
Why though?

2179
01:43:53,920 --> 01:43:55,920
Hey, the helicopter ran away!

2180
01:43:55,920 --> 01:43:57,720
Get back here!

2181
01:43:57,720 --> 01:43:58,720
Anything there?

2182
01:43:58,720 --> 01:44:03,920
No cameras

2183
01:44:03,920 --> 01:44:07,430
You need a camera?

2184
01:44:07,430 --> 01:44:09,430
Wait, do you have a physical CCTV camera?

2185
01:44:09,430 --> 01:44:12,230
I only had the one I gave you

2186
01:44:12,230 --> 01:44:14,230
How many do you need?

2187
01:44:14,230 --> 01:44:19,110
You need one to craft a homing missile

2188
01:44:19,110 --> 01:44:21,910
Wasn't the one I gave you enough?

2189
01:44:21,910 --> 01:44:24,710
I can make one, but not two

2190
01:44:24,710 --> 01:44:28,510
But we each have one now, thanks

2191
01:44:28,510 --> 01:44:33,110
I researched mine, so I only have one

2192
01:44:33,110 --> 01:44:35,020
Ah, that's why

2193
01:44:35,020 --> 01:44:35,910
So there's only one

2194
01:44:35,910 --> 01:44:37,710
Then let's fight with just the one

2195
01:44:39,510 --> 01:44:41,230
Let's do it together then

2196
01:44:41,230 --> 01:44:42,230
Yeah, let's

2197
01:44:42,230 --> 01:44:43,950
Yeah, yeah, let's do it

2198
01:44:43,950 --> 01:44:46,290
Yeah

2199
01:44:46,290 --> 01:44:49,610
There are still NPCs around

2200
01:44:49,610 --> 01:44:51,410
Watch out over there

2201
01:44:51,410 --> 01:44:54,980
Where's the NPC?

2202
01:44:54,980 --> 01:44:57,000
Right in front

2203
01:44:57,000 --> 01:45:01,170
Got it

2204
01:45:01,170 --> 01:45:02,460
What? A genius?

2205
01:45:02,460 --> 01:45:06,480
Hmm...

2206
01:45:06,480 --> 01:45:09,320
There's just the one

2207
01:45:10,180 --> 01:45:14,520
The homing missile

2208
01:45:14,520 --> 01:45:18,740
But the helicopter flew off somewhere

2209
01:45:18,740 --> 01:45:23,440
Let's just get ready for it. Oh, if it doesn't come, I'll use the M249

2210
01:45:23,440 --> 01:45:27,400
OK OK OK, get in, Polka

2211
01:45:27,400 --> 01:45:32,180
Polka's shooting? Yeah, use the homing missile — it'll track at this range

2212
01:45:32,180 --> 01:45:38,940
It didn't hit before, but Polka's shooting now. It's homing, so it should track

2213
01:45:38,940 --> 01:45:40,940
Really?

2214
01:45:40,940 --> 01:45:43,460
Otherwise why would they call it homing, right?

2215
01:45:43,460 --> 01:45:44,500
Give me ammo

2216
01:45:44,500 --> 01:45:48,500
Oh, I have ammo

2217
01:45:48,500 --> 01:45:54,200
No, not that way, not that way!

2218
01:45:54,200 --> 01:45:57,080
Is it coming? Did it come?

2219
01:45:57,080 --> 01:46:01,850
That beautiful face of yours—

2220
01:46:01,850 --> 01:46:06,180
The M249, this is it

2221
01:46:06,180 --> 01:46:08,040
Whoa, this is insane, what is this

2222
01:46:08,040 --> 01:46:10,200
I want to see it first

2223
01:46:15,740 --> 01:46:21,780
I'll do it away from the house. So Niko-tan doesn't get caught in the crossfire

2224
01:46:21,780 --> 01:46:24,240
Where? There's a horse here

2225
01:46:24,240 --> 01:46:26,610
Where is it?

2226
01:46:26,610 --> 01:46:31,030
Where is it? Why now of all times — ow ow ow ow

2227
01:46:31,030 --> 01:46:35,610
It's way over by the snow, that's really far

2228
01:46:35,610 --> 01:46:40,670
We need to get a bit closer. How do you lock on? Lock-on

2229
01:46:40,670 --> 01:46:43,730
Can you lock on if it gets closer?

2230
01:46:43,730 --> 01:46:45,620
Oh, you're right

2231
01:46:45,620 --> 01:46:47,250
It says "LOCK"

2232
01:46:47,250 --> 01:46:48,870
Oh, I see

2233
01:46:48,870 --> 01:46:51,270
Why does it never come when you actually need it, seriously

2234
01:46:51,270 --> 01:46:53,470
Shoot it, Kanatan

2235
01:46:53,470 --> 01:46:55,790
Hold on, I can't see it

2236
01:46:55,790 --> 01:46:56,830
Hmm

2237
01:46:56,830 --> 01:46:58,310
It's really far

2238
01:46:58,310 --> 01:47:00,710
It went off toward the Nuke area

2239
01:47:00,710 --> 01:47:06,010
J, I, 16? Are you kidding me

2240
01:47:07,290 --> 01:47:09,290
Why?! Why?!

2241
01:47:09,290 --> 01:47:11,750
It was chasing us so relentlessly before

2242
01:47:11,750 --> 01:47:14,150
"Did it sense the danger?"

2243
01:47:14,150 --> 01:47:19,340
It can tell when things are dangerous

2244
01:47:19,340 --> 01:47:24,450
Did it figure out we have homing missiles?

2245
01:47:24,450 --> 01:47:27,570
It knows us too well

2246
01:47:27,570 --> 01:47:29,670
It went completely the other way

2247
01:47:29,670 --> 01:47:30,370
It's just heading home like that

2248
01:47:30,370 --> 01:47:31,830
Oh wait, it suddenly turned back

2249
01:47:31,830 --> 01:47:33,840
"Is it coming?"

2250
01:47:33,870 --> 01:47:37,110
The direction feels like it might come this way

2251
01:47:37,110 --> 01:47:38,530
A laser?

2252
01:47:38,530 --> 01:47:45,490
Hey, stop ghosting us, helicopter!

2253
01:47:45,490 --> 01:47:46,830
Oh, I can use the scope too

2254
01:47:46,830 --> 01:47:50,550
You can hear it from that far away?

2255
01:47:50,550 --> 01:47:58,700
It's heading toward Water Treatment

2256
01:48:02,470 --> 01:48:05,850
Where did the heli go?

2257
01:48:05,850 --> 01:48:07,990
Right now it's at J, E, 13

2258
01:48:07,990 --> 01:48:10,450
That's really far

2259
01:48:10,450 --> 01:48:12,110
What's up?

2260
01:48:12,110 --> 01:48:13,430
Oh, it's not coming this way

2261
01:48:13,430 --> 01:48:15,150
What's going on?

2262
01:48:15,150 --> 01:48:17,350
It's scared

2263
01:48:17,350 --> 01:48:22,250
It's scared of us

2264
01:48:22,250 --> 01:48:23,290
Hmm...

2265
01:48:23,290 --> 01:48:28,670
It got scared all of a sudden

2266
01:48:28,670 --> 01:48:31,470
Oh, that's a good angle of approach

2267
01:48:31,470 --> 01:48:35,770
Got a lock!

2268
01:48:35,770 --> 01:48:39,530
Hmm, hmm...

2269
01:48:39,530 --> 01:48:44,810
Niko might get spooked again off-stream

2270
01:48:44,810 --> 01:48:47,350
Where's the heli sound?

2271
01:48:47,350 --> 01:48:49,940
It's getting closer!

2272
01:48:49,940 --> 01:48:54,420
Oh but it's homing, so it'll track

2273
01:48:54,420 --> 01:48:56,760
How close do we need to be for it to work?

2274
01:48:56,760 --> 01:49:00,100
It's flying, but you probably need to be in roughly the same grid square

2275
01:49:00,100 --> 01:49:01,660
What?!

2276
01:49:01,660 --> 01:49:03,900
That's super close!

2277
01:49:03,900 --> 01:49:04,800
Bathroom?

2278
01:49:04,800 --> 01:49:06,360
I went ahead and fired, Kanatan's in the bathroom

2279
01:49:06,360 --> 01:49:11,870
I just took a shot, but she's in the bathroom

2280
01:49:11,870 --> 01:49:17,500
Hahaha

2281
01:49:17,500 --> 01:49:18,500
It's a bit far though

2282
01:49:18,500 --> 01:49:21,500
Now I'm the one chasing you, heli!

2283
01:49:21,500 --> 01:49:25,300
Now it's your turn to be chased — brace yourself!

2284
01:49:25,300 --> 01:49:30,660
The lock-on is strong though

2285
01:49:30,660 --> 01:49:33,460
I really want to see the missile fire

2286
01:49:33,460 --> 01:49:35,460
Right, same

2287
01:49:35,460 --> 01:49:38,260
Patrol helicopter...

2288
01:49:38,260 --> 01:49:41,060
Huh? What's it doing... wait?

2289
01:49:41,060 --> 01:49:43,860
Huh? Where'd it go?

2290
01:49:44,700 --> 01:49:47,480
It went off to the sea on the right

2291
01:49:47,480 --> 01:49:53,200
We've got no vehicles left at all

2292
01:49:53,200 --> 01:49:57,040
Seriously?

2293
01:49:57,040 --> 01:50:00,820
Seeing that car marked as irreparable was a bit of a shock

2294
01:50:00,820 --> 01:50:03,840
I thought it just couldn't be fixed

2295
01:50:03,840 --> 01:50:05,420
We got wrecked

2296
01:50:05,420 --> 01:50:08,940
I can't even spot Polka on the map anymore

2297
01:50:08,940 --> 01:50:11,860
Is it retreating?

2298
01:50:13,040 --> 01:50:14,680
Did it lose? Did the heli lose?

2299
01:50:14,680 --> 01:50:15,820
Ugh...

2300
01:50:15,820 --> 01:50:16,640
It admitted defeat

2301
01:50:16,640 --> 01:50:18,640
Yeah, it stopped coming

2302
01:50:18,640 --> 01:50:19,640
Phew...

2303
01:50:19,640 --> 01:50:22,140
Phew...

2304
01:50:22,140 --> 01:50:24,240
We still have the bicycle

2305
01:50:24,240 --> 01:50:27,040
Yeah, the bicycle is literally all we have left

2306
01:50:27,040 --> 01:50:28,040
A bicycle and a horse

2307
01:50:28,040 --> 01:50:30,040
Look on the bright side — at least we have a bicycle

2308
01:50:30,040 --> 01:50:34,840
Well, there is a way to fully recover from this

2309
01:50:34,840 --> 01:50:35,840
Technically

2310
01:50:35,840 --> 01:50:37,640
If we just hammer away at it

2311
01:50:37,640 --> 01:50:38,640
It should fix, right?

2312
01:50:38,640 --> 01:50:40,940
Well, uh, yeah, hmm, I wonder

2313
01:50:40,940 --> 01:50:43,390
Oh, it won't fix. It's completely destroyed

2314
01:50:43,390 --> 01:50:46,900
Yeah, the body itself is broken — we'll have to find another one somewhere

2315
01:50:46,900 --> 01:50:48,700
Yeah this is done, it's broken

2316
01:50:48,700 --> 01:50:52,850
It might have still been okay a little while ago

2317
01:50:52,850 --> 01:50:59,760
Well, that's that. It's over then

2318
01:50:59,760 --> 01:51:03,580
It's gone. Well, if we play tonight, it'll be the heli

2319
01:51:03,580 --> 01:51:05,560
Yeah, for sure

2320
01:51:05,560 --> 01:51:09,380
If we play tonight, it's gotta be the heli

2321
01:51:09,380 --> 01:51:14,300
By the way, can you craft homing missile ammo?

2322
01:51:14,300 --> 01:51:17,960
Hmm, I'm not sure

2323
01:51:17,960 --> 01:51:27,960
Let me look it up real quick. We only have 9 homing missiles anyway

2324
01:51:28,400 --> 01:51:33,950
Only 9? Well, 9 is still something

2325
01:51:33,950 --> 01:51:41,200
Oh, this item can't be crafted from scrap. Huh...

2326
01:51:41,800 --> 01:51:44,080
Even though it's a homing missile?

2327
01:51:44,080 --> 01:51:48,170
Do we have to craft it somewhere else?

2328
01:51:48,170 --> 01:51:50,370
Wait, is this a missile?

2329
01:51:50,370 --> 01:51:53,610
Which one is the homing one?

2330
01:51:53,610 --> 01:51:55,730
The one called Homing Missile

2331
01:51:55,730 --> 01:51:57,310
Oh, the Homing Missile Launcher is the one that—

2332
01:51:57,310 --> 01:51:59,150
Needs a CCTV camera, right?

2333
01:51:59,150 --> 01:52:00,190
This one?

2334
01:52:00,190 --> 01:52:01,430
Yeah, yeah, that's the one

2335
01:52:01,430 --> 01:52:04,930
Let me see if I can research the ammo

2336
01:52:04,930 --> 01:52:09,910
Oh, it's already been researched

2337
01:52:09,910 --> 01:52:10,750
We can craft it

2338
01:52:10,750 --> 01:52:12,250
Oh nice, you already unlocked it, good job

2339
01:52:12,250 --> 01:52:14,250
Should we craft a bunch of them?

2340
01:52:14,250 --> 01:52:17,120
Yeah...

2341
01:52:17,120 --> 01:52:21,120
We've really done everything we could today

2342
01:52:21,120 --> 01:52:23,920
We gotta use them today though

2343
01:52:23,920 --> 01:52:25,720
For real?

2344
01:52:25,720 --> 01:52:27,720
Pipes... we need pipes again?

2345
01:52:27,720 --> 01:52:29,720
Pipes, gunpowder, and junk

2346
01:52:29,720 --> 01:52:33,520
We're running low on pipes too

2347
01:52:33,520 --> 01:52:35,520
Pipes, gunpowder, and junk

2348
01:52:35,520 --> 01:52:38,360
I'll craft the homing ammo

2349
01:52:38,360 --> 01:52:42,200
Homing missiles

2350
01:52:42,200 --> 01:52:48,890
They say 9 is enough, but I'd rather craft more launchers

2351
01:52:48,890 --> 01:52:54,490
Yeah, we need more launchers. I want another launcher

2352
01:52:54,490 --> 01:52:58,230
We need to find a camera first. Right

2353
01:52:58,230 --> 01:53:06,490
Can we do it now? The fact that we've gotten to the point of crafting launchers is kind of scary

2354
01:53:06,490 --> 01:53:11,330
Good work today. We might need to find a CCTV camera

2355
01:53:11,330 --> 01:53:17,030
I never even thought about crafting a launcher before. Even now

2356
01:53:17,030 --> 01:53:24,170
I wonder if we have any

2357
01:53:24,170 --> 01:53:28,610
Hmm. This is a hatch, right?

2358
01:53:28,610 --> 01:53:33,990
What should I do with Kanata's stuff? I already tidied it up

2359
01:53:35,310 --> 01:53:38,030
Oh, maybe the shop sells them

2360
01:53:38,030 --> 01:53:40,650
CCTV cameras~

2361
01:53:40,650 --> 01:53:43,410
What's the most expensive thing you can buy at the shop?

2362
01:53:43,410 --> 01:53:47,640
Probably the helicopter, right?

2363
01:53:47,640 --> 01:53:48,980
The helicopter, huh

2364
01:53:48,980 --> 01:53:50,880
The large helicopter~

2365
01:53:50,880 --> 01:53:56,230
I'm riding the large helicopter~

2366
01:54:02,500 --> 01:54:05,640
I wonder if they have any

2367
01:54:08,470 --> 01:54:11,470
Do we have to go all the way to Bandit Camp?

2368
01:54:11,470 --> 01:54:12,270
Hmm

2369
01:54:12,270 --> 01:54:16,270
Well, we do have a helicopter at our base

2370
01:54:16,270 --> 01:54:18,270
We have a helicopter, but...

2371
01:54:18,270 --> 01:54:21,070
We've got a helicopter

2372
01:54:21,070 --> 01:54:22,070
We've got a helicopter

2373
01:54:22,070 --> 01:54:26,070
No CCTV cameras

2374
01:54:26,070 --> 01:54:29,150
None? They don't sell them?

2375
01:54:29,150 --> 01:54:32,590
What about your helicopter?

2376
01:54:32,590 --> 01:54:36,390
The helicopter's okay, but landing is pretty tricky

2377
01:54:36,390 --> 01:54:40,190
If we take the heli, it'd be super fast

2378
01:54:40,190 --> 01:54:45,190
True, but I don't really want to fly it

2379
01:54:45,190 --> 01:54:47,990
It'd be so quick by heli, so why not?

2380
01:54:47,990 --> 01:54:54,730
For getting around, it's either a bike, a horse, or the heli

2381
01:54:54,730 --> 01:55:00,760
Just fly there, it's easy

2382
01:55:00,760 --> 01:55:03,570
Landing is the problem

2383
01:55:03,570 --> 01:55:07,020
Polka doesn't know how

2384
01:55:07,020 --> 01:55:08,960
Why don't you try flying it, Polka?

2385
01:55:08,960 --> 01:55:11,580
I'm telling you, I'd crash it instantly

2386
01:55:11,580 --> 01:55:15,900
It's fine, we have 5,000 scrap

2387
01:55:15,900 --> 01:55:19,320
Amazing. Then teach her, Luna!

2388
01:55:19,320 --> 01:55:23,070
Give her a full lesson! Let's do it in the morning

2389
01:55:23,070 --> 01:55:25,440
It's all about the feel. Getting used to flying it

2390
01:55:25,440 --> 01:55:29,460
Teach her, teach her!

2391
01:55:29,460 --> 01:55:32,360
It takes a bit of energy

2392
01:55:32,360 --> 01:55:37,860
Hmm...

2393
01:55:37,860 --> 01:55:40,260
I definitely don't need this, but I'll put it here anyway

2394
01:55:40,260 --> 01:55:48,100
The heli stopped coming

2395
01:55:48,100 --> 01:55:49,900
The heli already left

2396
01:55:49,900 --> 01:55:53,000
Until we get the notification that it's spawned again

2397
01:55:53,000 --> 01:55:53,800
The heli too

2398
01:55:53,800 --> 01:55:55,840
Why does the heli always do this

2399
01:55:55,840 --> 01:55:57,700
It was so sudden

2400
01:55:57,700 --> 01:55:59,700
It left because we stopped

2401
01:55:59,700 --> 01:56:02,400
The moment I said "let's do this," it left

2402
01:56:03,200 --> 01:56:05,200
I hate that about it

2403
01:56:05,200 --> 01:56:06,200
Seriously though

2404
01:56:06,200 --> 01:56:07,200
Right?

2405
01:56:07,200 --> 01:56:10,000
It's totally playing us

2406
01:56:10,000 --> 01:56:18,820
We could build a new car from scratch, but...

2407
01:56:18,820 --> 01:56:22,310
I'm a little rusty on how to do it

2408
01:56:22,310 --> 01:56:31,710
Wanna take the mini-heli?

2409
01:56:31,710 --> 01:56:33,650
Aren't we taking the mini-heli?

2410
01:56:33,650 --> 01:56:35,450
Where are we going?

2411
01:56:36,270 --> 01:56:41,030
I'm not sure I can fly it, but if we're going, where was it again?

2412
01:56:41,030 --> 01:56:44,490
If we're going, what was the place again?

2413
01:56:44,490 --> 01:56:46,550
That's scary

2414
01:56:46,550 --> 01:56:48,130
The Bandit Camp, right?

2415
01:56:48,130 --> 01:56:52,430
We're going shopping

2416
01:56:52,430 --> 01:56:56,170
This is at a tricky angle

2417
01:56:56,170 --> 01:56:59,050
There's a chance it might fall

2418
01:56:59,050 --> 01:57:01,590
Oh, Niko-tan will clean it up?

2419
01:57:01,590 --> 01:57:03,850
Oh, can Polka do it?

2420
01:57:03,850 --> 01:57:05,090
Oh, no, I can't

2421
01:57:05,090 --> 01:57:07,260
I was wondering what you were going to do

2422
01:57:07,260 --> 01:57:10,130
Worth a try though

2423
01:57:10,130 --> 01:57:13,640
Even though I can't do it

2424
01:57:13,640 --> 01:57:16,500
Should I not bring the M249?

2425
01:57:16,500 --> 01:57:16,940
Yeah

2426
01:57:16,940 --> 01:57:20,500
Leave it at home

2427
01:57:20,500 --> 01:57:22,700
Might crash

2428
01:57:22,700 --> 01:57:23,120
Yeah

2429
01:57:23,120 --> 01:57:25,980
Okay

2430
01:57:25,980 --> 01:57:34,600
Just getting it out is hard enough

2431
01:57:34,600 --> 01:57:36,880
Push, push, push

2432
01:57:36,880 --> 01:57:38,940
Push, push, push, push

2433
01:57:38,940 --> 01:57:42,080
So while you're in it, use the controller to...

2434
01:57:42,080 --> 01:57:48,010
You go up, right?

2435
01:57:48,010 --> 01:57:51,260
There was no fuel in it

2436
01:57:51,260 --> 01:57:55,100
Put fuel in and get on

2437
01:57:55,100 --> 01:58:01,850
With the controller

2438
01:58:08,290 --> 01:58:10,020
Oh!

2439
01:58:10,020 --> 01:58:12,010
I can see an airdrop

2440
01:58:12,010 --> 01:58:13,920
Okay

2441
01:58:13,920 --> 01:58:15,920
Nothing?

2442
01:58:15,920 --> 01:58:17,720
Don't just say "okay"

2443
01:58:17,720 --> 01:58:19,720
When you're flying, um...

2444
01:58:19,720 --> 01:58:21,320
Hold W and...

2445
01:58:21,320 --> 01:58:23,320
You hold it to go up

2446
01:58:23,320 --> 01:58:25,320
So holding W makes you go up?

2447
01:58:25,320 --> 01:58:27,120
Wait, I can break it?

2448
01:58:27,120 --> 01:58:29,010
You want me to drive now?

2449
01:58:29,010 --> 01:58:30,920
Alright then, you're driving!

2450
01:58:30,920 --> 01:58:32,920
Let's go!

2451
01:58:32,920 --> 01:58:34,720
I've been waiting for this!

2452
01:58:34,720 --> 01:58:38,940
Wait, I thought I left the M249 behind but I still have it

2453
01:58:38,940 --> 01:58:43,450
Let me give it to Kanata

2454
01:58:43,450 --> 01:58:44,770
No wait

2455
01:58:44,770 --> 01:58:47,090
Oh, I put down a different one

2456
01:58:47,090 --> 01:58:48,870
Let me store it with Kanata

2457
01:58:48,870 --> 01:58:49,750
The M249

2458
01:58:49,750 --> 01:58:53,110
This is the M249

2459
01:58:53,110 --> 01:58:53,430
Okay

2460
01:58:53,430 --> 01:58:57,570
Here

2461
01:58:57,570 --> 01:59:00,670
Hah

2462
01:59:00,670 --> 01:59:02,250
Alright

2463
01:59:02,250 --> 01:59:05,650
Is it here?

2464
01:59:05,650 --> 01:59:07,450
Uh, yeah, I think so

2465
01:59:07,450 --> 01:59:09,450
The Bandit Camp, Bandit Camp

2466
01:59:09,450 --> 01:59:11,250
More or less

2467
01:59:11,250 --> 01:59:13,250
I forgot how to do this

2468
01:59:13,250 --> 01:59:15,250
Isn't it straight ahead? Wait, where is it?

2469
01:59:15,250 --> 01:59:17,050
The Bandit Camp is...

2470
01:59:17,050 --> 01:59:19,730
One-day trip to the Bandit Camp

2471
01:59:19,730 --> 01:59:21,730
Oh, hold on

2472
01:59:21,730 --> 01:59:23,530
What the—!?

2473
01:59:23,530 --> 01:59:25,530
The rotor, the rotor hit something

2474
01:59:25,530 --> 01:59:30,590
It's roughly in the N, north direction

2475
01:59:30,590 --> 01:59:32,590
Oh~! Nice, nice!

2476
01:59:32,590 --> 01:59:34,390
Wow, you're good at this!

2477
01:59:34,390 --> 01:59:36,710
Right, Hime?

2478
01:59:36,710 --> 01:59:43,590
I can at least go up, and going up is important — but going straight too, amazing

2479
01:59:43,590 --> 01:59:48,910
The angle looks great too, she's keeping it level and moving backward — you're doing great, Hime

2480
01:59:48,910 --> 01:59:55,050
You need to go forward — this is the old mini-heli, I can do it when someone's guiding me

2481
01:59:55,050 --> 02:00:00,870
Hmm, well done, Hime!

2482
02:00:00,870 --> 02:00:03,640
There!

2483
02:00:03,760 --> 02:00:10,940
I can see the airdrop clearly. The flying part looks good — it's the landing that's scary.

2484
02:00:10,940 --> 02:00:18,860
Well, they say takeoff and landing are the most dangerous parts of flying. So true.

2485
02:00:18,860 --> 02:00:22,960
But wait — isn't she actually pretty good?

2486
02:00:22,960 --> 02:00:25,080
Right? Yeah.

2487
02:00:25,080 --> 02:00:30,540
Wait, she's — where did she learn this? Isn't this amazing?

2488
02:00:30,540 --> 02:00:31,740
Self-taught.

2489
02:00:31,740 --> 02:00:33,200
Isn't that incredible? Isn't she good?

2490
02:00:33,200 --> 02:00:34,200
What?!

2491
02:00:34,200 --> 02:00:38,950
But...

2492
02:00:38,950 --> 02:00:40,350
Where is she?

2493
02:00:40,350 --> 02:00:41,570
She's getting closer.

2494
02:00:41,570 --> 02:00:46,440
Where should I land this thing?

2495
02:00:46,440 --> 02:00:48,160
Where's the safe zone exactly?

2496
02:00:48,160 --> 02:00:49,640
Can the heli get shot down here?

2497
02:00:49,640 --> 02:00:52,360
Apparently not here.

2498
02:00:52,360 --> 02:00:53,300
Oh, okay then.

2499
02:00:53,300 --> 02:00:55,200
Something like this should be fine, right?

2500
02:00:55,200 --> 02:00:57,720
Oh, she's getting closer and closer.

2501
02:00:57,720 --> 02:00:59,560
Whoa...

2502
02:00:59,560 --> 02:01:01,580
Yes! That's it, that's it, that's it!

2503
02:01:01,580 --> 02:01:03,580
Great job!

2504
02:01:03,380 --> 02:01:05,380
So good, so good, so good!

2505
02:01:05,380 --> 02:01:08,580
Ow! Oh wait, huh?

2506
02:01:08,580 --> 02:01:10,580
It broke lol

2507
02:01:10,580 --> 02:01:12,580
Ow!

2508
02:01:13,070 --> 02:01:14,580
It's fine, we can repair this, right?

2509
02:01:14,580 --> 02:01:17,580
Totally. Did it hit a rock or something?

2510
02:01:17,580 --> 02:01:19,580
Yeah. It's the rock's fault.

2511
02:01:19,580 --> 02:01:21,580
The rock's fault. It shouldn't have been there. It shouldn't have been there.

2512
02:01:21,580 --> 02:01:24,580
You did great! That was great!

2513
02:01:24,580 --> 02:01:27,580
Wait, it made a big crash sound — is it okay?

2514
02:01:27,580 --> 02:01:31,300
Seriously? It's fine, it's fine. That was just, um—

2515
02:01:31,100 --> 02:01:35,600
That was, what do you call it — a performance.

2516
02:01:35,600 --> 02:01:41,450
That was a performance, see? It's totally fine, look how clean it is.

2517
02:01:41,450 --> 02:01:43,010
Oh, it's okay — it's fixed.

2518
02:01:43,010 --> 02:01:44,530
Wow!

2519
02:01:44,530 --> 02:01:47,250
Somehow pulled it off!

2520
02:01:47,250 --> 02:01:49,290
"Somehow pulled it off" — you...

2521
02:01:49,290 --> 02:01:54,830
You've grown so much at so many things, Hime.

2522
02:01:54,830 --> 02:01:58,290
This whole Rust session—

2523
02:01:58,290 --> 02:02:02,590
It's been a story of trying all kinds of things and getting better.

2524
02:02:02,590 --> 02:02:05,030
Ouch!

2525
02:02:05,030 --> 02:02:10,390
Do you have any CCTV cameras? You said they weren't selling them.

2526
02:02:10,390 --> 02:02:17,410
Don't you have any? Aren't you selling what I need?

2527
02:02:17,410 --> 02:02:23,880
Nope, nothing. You can't buy what isn't there.

2528
02:02:23,880 --> 02:02:25,680
Nothing, huh.

2529
02:02:25,680 --> 02:02:28,560
What did we come here for again?

2530
02:02:28,560 --> 02:02:31,480
To see if they sell CCTV cameras.

2531
02:02:31,480 --> 02:02:33,480
They probably don't, do they?

2532
02:02:33,480 --> 02:02:35,480
I might have missed it.

2533
02:02:35,480 --> 02:02:38,280
There might be something.

2534
02:02:38,280 --> 02:02:40,280
There's nobody around.

2535
02:02:40,280 --> 02:02:45,380
I've never actually bought a CCTV camera before, so I don't even know where to look.

2536
02:02:45,380 --> 02:02:51,370
Yeah, we never needed to buy one before.

2537
02:02:51,370 --> 02:02:59,670
What about a practice heli for Polka?

2538
02:02:59,670 --> 02:03:06,270
I brought 2,800 scrap, so I can buy one.

2539
02:03:06,270 --> 02:03:09,870
Polka, over here!

2540
02:03:09,870 --> 02:03:13,470
Wares, wares!

2541
02:03:13,470 --> 02:03:16,470
Oh wow, this brings back memories.

2542
02:03:16,470 --> 02:03:24,510
Anyway, you can buy the usual stuff here — Polka, come on in.

2543
02:03:24,510 --> 02:03:30,730
You can buy one for me — let's see, aircraft...

2544
02:03:30,730 --> 02:03:35,750
The smallest heli — mini-heli, 750. Thank you!

2545
02:03:35,750 --> 02:03:43,050
Flying the transport heli is way too scary. Here, giving it back — I'm scared.

2546
02:03:43,050 --> 02:03:44,850
Teach me how to fly it!

2547
02:03:44,850 --> 02:03:48,850
Okay, so — mouse movements should be really slow and gentle.

2548
02:03:48,850 --> 02:03:51,650
Wait, first of all, how do I go up?

2549
02:03:51,650 --> 02:03:58,500
Press W to start the engine, hold W to go up, and S to go down.

2550
02:03:58,500 --> 02:04:08,250
To change direction, use A or D to turn, and use the mouse to keep it level — tilt forward and

2551
02:04:08,250 --> 02:04:14,350
you'll move forward. So tilting the mouse up makes you lean forward — like this.

2552
02:04:14,350 --> 02:04:23,610
I'm going up! I'm going way up, but I went up — what do I do now?

2553
02:04:23,610 --> 02:04:29,070
To move forward, tilt the mouse up slightly and

2554
02:04:29,070 --> 02:04:35,850
you'll go forward. If you're going backward, it means you're tilting the mouse down,

2555
02:04:35,850 --> 02:04:40,370
so tilt it up — up.

2556
02:04:40,370 --> 02:04:43,350
What are you even saying?

2557
02:04:43,350 --> 02:04:47,670
Well, you just have to get a feel for it.

2558
02:04:47,670 --> 02:04:52,530
Tilt it a little — which direction am I facing?

2559
02:04:52,530 --> 02:04:55,720
This direction?

2560
02:04:56,360 --> 02:04:59,000
But you seem to be doing okay, right?

2561
02:04:59,000 --> 02:05:00,700
I'm going backwards, I'm going backwards!

2562
02:05:00,700 --> 02:05:02,720
What do I do when I'm going backwards?

2563
02:05:02,720 --> 02:05:05,360
Move the mouse up, flick it upward

2564
02:05:05,360 --> 02:05:07,540
If you flick it up, you'll go forward

2565
02:05:07,540 --> 02:05:10,120
You're going backwards when you flick it

2566
02:05:10,120 --> 02:05:12,080
Mouse up, UP, UP!

2567
02:05:12,080 --> 02:05:14,020
What do you mean by up—

2568
02:05:14,020 --> 02:05:17,740
Wait, I'm going backwards?

2569
02:05:17,740 --> 02:05:20,860
Like, flick the mouse up, up, up

2570
02:05:20,860 --> 02:05:22,160
Flick it upward

2571
02:05:22,160 --> 02:05:23,700
Flick it upward

2572
02:05:23,700 --> 02:05:25,700
Huh? But when I go up I go backwards...

2573
02:05:25,700 --> 02:05:27,400
Is it reversed?

2574
02:05:27,400 --> 02:05:29,300
Did I already mess it up?

2575
02:05:29,300 --> 02:05:32,900
Oh, it's toward you — pull it toward you

2576
02:05:32,900 --> 02:05:34,000
Toward me?

2577
02:05:34,000 --> 02:05:35,000
Yeah, toward you

2578
02:05:35,000 --> 02:05:40,120
Huh? But I'm still going backwards?

2579
02:05:40,120 --> 02:05:42,120
I can't really tell without actually flying it

2580
02:05:42,120 --> 02:05:42,820
Huh?

2581
02:05:42,820 --> 02:05:44,020
Wait, was it backwards?

2582
02:05:44,020 --> 02:05:45,220
Hold on — ahhh!

2583
02:05:45,220 --> 02:05:47,220
Too close, too close, too close — hold on, ahhh!

2584
02:05:47,220 --> 02:05:49,120
Too close — everything's too close, especially the ground

2585
02:05:49,120 --> 02:05:50,620
Where did Pol go?

2586
02:05:50,620 --> 02:05:52,420
Ahh, I fell!

2587
02:05:52,420 --> 02:05:54,420
Polka fell!!

2588
02:05:54,420 --> 02:05:56,420
Polka fell??

2589
02:05:56,420 --> 02:06:00,260
What happened?

2590
02:06:00,260 --> 02:06:03,080
Where even is this?

2591
02:06:03,080 --> 02:06:07,020
How far did Polka fly?

2592
02:06:07,020 --> 02:06:09,020
She went pretty far

2593
02:06:09,020 --> 02:06:11,020
She ended up all the way to the north

2594
02:06:11,020 --> 02:06:13,020
Polka's really bad at going forward

2595
02:06:13,020 --> 02:06:15,020
How do you even go forward?

2596
02:06:15,020 --> 02:06:16,820
And somehow I survived

2597
02:06:16,820 --> 02:06:21,400
I can't really figure it out unless I'm actually flying

2598
02:06:22,300 --> 02:06:25,180
I'm just bad at going forward

2599
02:06:25,180 --> 02:06:26,900
I keep going backwards

2600
02:06:26,900 --> 02:06:28,080
She didn't die?

2601
02:06:28,080 --> 02:06:34,590
Just now, with the ground—

2602
02:06:34,590 --> 02:06:36,190
I thought I was pretty close and

2603
02:06:36,190 --> 02:06:38,570
She hit Space and died

2604
02:06:38,570 --> 02:06:39,490
Just like that

2605
02:06:39,490 --> 02:06:41,670
I see, I accidentally hit Space

2606
02:06:41,670 --> 02:06:44,130
It's on fire — good thing I didn't crash into someone's house

2607
02:06:44,130 --> 02:06:47,720
Well, but—

2608
02:06:47,720 --> 02:06:54,000
The whole pushing the mouse forward thing

2609
02:06:54,000 --> 02:06:56,000
I still don't really get it

2610
02:06:56,000 --> 02:07:00,400
Does forward mean pulling it toward me, or

2611
02:07:00,400 --> 02:07:02,100
Pushing it away?

2612
02:07:02,100 --> 02:07:03,640
Pushing it away?

2613
02:07:03,640 --> 02:07:06,760
Wait, where did the helicopter go?

2614
02:07:06,760 --> 02:07:10,630
There it is

2615
02:07:10,630 --> 02:07:14,830
Push it away? But even then

2616
02:07:14,830 --> 02:07:16,730
It doesn't work right

2617
02:07:16,730 --> 02:07:19,570
Maybe I'm not keeping it level?

2618
02:07:19,570 --> 02:07:23,090
So, W makes you ascend

2619
02:07:23,090 --> 02:07:23,750
Yeah

2620
02:07:23,750 --> 02:07:33,050
Then tilt the mouse up like this and you should move forward

2621
02:07:33,050 --> 02:07:34,350
Like this

2622
02:07:34,350 --> 02:07:35,070
Hmm

2623
02:07:35,070 --> 02:07:41,830
Where's Poh-Poh?

2624
02:07:41,830 --> 02:07:51,830
Going backwards is probably because the mouse is sliding down

2625
02:07:53,840 --> 02:07:56,740
Maybe I need to keep pushing it more and more forward?

2626
02:08:02,320 --> 02:08:05,880
It's tricky, even the controls at speed

2627
02:08:05,880 --> 02:08:10,380
I remembered to do it just a little, but then doing just a little

2628
02:08:10,380 --> 02:08:14,000
I kept drifting further and further back

2629
02:08:14,000 --> 02:08:16,200
Ugh, this is hard

2630
02:08:16,200 --> 02:08:18,020
This is seriously difficult

2631
02:08:18,020 --> 02:08:21,360
It really is hard — Polka has never once gotten it right

2632
02:08:21,360 --> 02:08:22,600
With the helicopter

2633
02:08:22,600 --> 02:08:27,820
Maybe she's coming to pick me up

2634
02:08:27,820 --> 02:08:29,420
Whoa, amazing

2635
02:08:29,420 --> 02:08:30,520
Coming to pick me up—

2636
02:08:30,520 --> 02:08:33,060
Someone's coming to pick me up by helicopter

2637
02:08:33,060 --> 02:08:34,020
By helicopter

2638
02:08:34,020 --> 02:08:35,700
She came by helicopter

2639
02:08:35,700 --> 02:08:40,510
Where is this?

2640
02:08:40,510 --> 02:08:42,870
Whoa, here it is!

2641
02:08:42,870 --> 02:08:44,530
Whoa, there it is!

2642
02:08:44,530 --> 02:08:45,990
Around here.

2643
02:08:45,990 --> 02:08:48,770
That's amazing!

2644
02:08:48,770 --> 02:08:50,210
The people who are good at this—

2645
02:08:50,210 --> 02:08:55,920
I wonder how many missiles the attack helicopter fires.

2646
02:08:55,920 --> 02:08:59,200
The attack helicopter looks really hard.

2647
02:08:59,200 --> 02:08:59,960
I wonder.

2648
02:08:59,960 --> 02:09:03,320
But there was a helicopter that could carry a lot of people, right?

2649
02:09:03,320 --> 02:09:05,700
One that fits a bunch of people.

2650
02:09:05,700 --> 02:09:08,550
There she is.

2651
02:09:08,550 --> 02:09:10,170
You can actually—

2652
02:09:10,170 --> 02:09:13,130
tilt it forward, right?

2653
02:09:13,130 --> 02:09:15,450
That's incredible.

2654
02:09:15,450 --> 02:09:18,290
So smooth, so smooth!

2655
02:09:18,290 --> 02:09:21,170
Luna is genuinely good at this.

2656
02:09:21,170 --> 02:09:24,410
To be flying this cleanly after just a few tries—

2657
02:09:24,410 --> 02:09:26,790
that's impressive.

2658
02:09:26,790 --> 02:09:28,290
Heh~

2659
02:09:28,290 --> 02:09:30,090
Want to fly it again?

2660
02:09:30,090 --> 02:09:30,590
Yeah.

2661
02:09:30,590 --> 02:09:32,590
If we die here it'll all be for nothing.

2662
02:09:32,590 --> 02:09:34,390
Way out here at the edge of the map—

2663
02:09:34,390 --> 02:09:36,390
if both of us die,

2664
02:09:36,390 --> 02:09:38,190
that'd be a disaster.

2665
02:09:38,190 --> 02:09:39,990
That was close.

2666
02:09:39,990 --> 02:09:41,790
Let's head back.

2667
02:09:41,790 --> 02:09:43,590
Okay!

2668
02:09:43,590 --> 02:09:45,090
Hmm, where is it—

2669
02:09:45,090 --> 02:09:47,890
That blue marker over here.

2670
02:09:47,890 --> 02:09:51,180
Yay!

2671
02:09:51,180 --> 02:09:54,520
With the controller—

2672
02:09:55,520 --> 02:10:00,220
Ascending now.

2673
02:10:00,220 --> 02:10:06,740
The world is visible.

2674
02:10:06,740 --> 02:10:13,370
I can see the island!

2675
02:10:13,370 --> 02:10:16,910
You can see it!

2676
02:10:16,910 --> 02:10:22,330
Slide up and then forward—

2677
02:10:22,330 --> 02:10:29,990
Oh, this is the feeling, I think — lean forward a bit — this is wild.

2678
02:10:29,990 --> 02:10:36,600
A ship!

2679
02:10:36,600 --> 02:10:39,460
Heli-a, heli-a!

2680
02:10:39,460 --> 02:10:43,550
Heli-a!

2681
02:10:43,550 --> 02:10:51,280
Our base is a bit more that way — same with the dome, right?

2682
02:10:51,400 --> 02:10:56,840
Just enough to move upward — something like that.

2683
02:10:56,840 --> 02:10:59,740
Wow, that's amazing, nice!

2684
02:10:59,740 --> 02:11:06,460
I think you can only go slowly — there's a lot going on.

2685
02:11:06,460 --> 02:11:16,460
You can see all the structures on the island — I can tell there were tons of people around the Bandit Camp. There's a lot over here.

2686
02:11:18,960 --> 02:11:22,730
There was a crazy amount of activity around the Bandit Camp.

2687
02:11:22,730 --> 02:11:32,570
You were flying pretty well just now.

2688
02:11:32,570 --> 02:11:38,370
Well, flying — or more like hovering.

2689
02:11:38,370 --> 02:11:42,370
But it's going the opposite direction from where I intended, so something's off again.

2690
02:11:42,370 --> 02:11:44,370
I said too much.

2691
02:11:44,370 --> 02:11:46,170
Home—

2692
02:11:46,170 --> 02:11:50,110
Home, home — not past it, just right.

2693
02:11:50,110 --> 02:11:52,910
Nice landing!

2694
02:11:52,910 --> 02:11:55,600
Even without being able to see below—

2695
02:11:55,600 --> 02:11:57,310
it looked like it was about to hit something.

2696
02:11:57,310 --> 02:11:59,310
That was a little scary.

2697
02:11:59,310 --> 02:12:01,110
The blades took a little damage.

2698
02:12:01,110 --> 02:12:03,110
Oh, looks okay, looks okay!

2699
02:12:03,110 --> 02:12:07,840
Nice!

2700
